{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01882eZNT13ugpX9KmjecdNA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — xling_calib_direction\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: **EACL 2027** (ARR submission deadline: August 3, 2026 — 10.5 weeks from project start)\n5\t- Core submission: 2 models × 20 languages × all contributions\n6\t- Camera-ready extension: Gemma 4 31B Dense + 30+ languages\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight\n9\tThe model's internal correctness direction occupies a language-agnostic low-dimensional subspace that persists even as global representations specialize by language (CKA declines with depth). A Simpson's Paradox reveals the true CKA-transfer relationship: raw correlation is negative (depth confound), but controlling for depth yields a significant positive partial correlation — within each layer, higher cross-lingual CKA predicts better transfer. This geometric insight, combined with the architecture-dependent depth-transferability tradeoff (strong on Qwen, weak on Llama), provides a structural explanation for when and why cross-lingual probe transfer succeeds or fails. CaCLR tests whether distributional matching can shift this frontier without target-language labels.\n10\t\n11\t## Core Claims (4, causal chain)\n12\t\n13\t### Claim 1 — Pareto Frontier (Discovery)\n14\tCross-lingual correctness probes reveal a depth-transferability tradeoff that varies across architectures: on some architectures (Qwen), deeper layers produce better English probes but consistently degrade in cross-lingual transfer (strong tradeoff); on others (Llama), the tradeoff is language-specific — some languages improve with depth while others plateau or degrade. Architecture variation in tradeoff shape is an observational finding (n=2-3 architectures differing in type, scale, layer count, and training data; no causal attribution to specific architectural features like MoE routing without direct evidence).\n15\t- MVP evidence: Qwen2.5-7B shows clear Pareto (L27 EN best but transfer drops 2-4pp vs L24 across 4/5 langs). Llama-3.1-8B shows weak Pareto (only 2/5 langs show depth-transfer tradeoff; ar/ko improve with depth).\n16\t- Full evidence: 2 large architectures × 20 languages × all layers × 5 transfer conditions. Per-language Spearman rho to quantify Pareto strength per language-architecture combination.\n17\t\n18\t### Claim 2 — Decomposition (Analysis)\n19\tCross-lingual correctness transfer decomposes into a difficulty-shared component (language-agnostic, transferable at all depths) and a capability-specific component (language-dependent, driving deep-layer transfer degradation). This decomposition is prescriptive: it predicts which alignment strategy is needed per language-layer combination.\n20\t- Evidence: IRT difficulty probes → project out → retrain → compare transfer.\n21\t\n22\t### Claim 3 — CaCLR (Method / Diagnostic)\n23\tCaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_consistency, where L_consistency uses MMD on probe logits computed from parallel inputs — English and target language versions of the same GlobalMMLU train-split items) tests whether joint calibration + cross-lingual invariance optimization can shift the Pareto frontier without target-language correctness labels. Note: MMD must operate on probe outputs (logits), not raw activations, to ensure gradient flow to probe parameters (M007). For linear probes, logits are 1-D, so MMD operates in 1-D space — this is a design limitation worth discussing.\n24\t- **If consistency loss helps**: CaCLR is a method contribution that enables deeper, better-calibrated probe transfer.\n25\t- **If consistency loss is inert**: The negative result itself is the contribution — demonstrating that MMD-based distributional matching fails for correctness probe transfer (scope to MMD specifically; acknowledge domain adaptation theory predicts marginal matching failure when conditional distributions differ, cite Zhao et al. 2019). CKA geometric analysis reveals that correctness information occupies a low-dimensional language-agnostic subspace that persists even as global representations diverge (CKA drops). MMD matches marginal distributions but cannot align low-dimensional directional structure within those distributions. Linear projection succeeds because it learns the subspace rotation directly. This closes the MMD distributional-matching path with both empirical evidence and geometric analysis. **Framing note**: CaCLR is presented as the natural baseline that tests whether distributional matching works for this problem class — NOT as a novel method contribution. Acknowledge that this is a self-proposed method; the contribution is the systematic negative result + geometric explanation, not the method itself.\n26\t- **Implementation specification (MUST report for reproducibility)**: MMD kernel (Gaussian RBF with median heuristic bandwidth), optimizer (Adam), learning rate, epochs, early stopping criterion, initialization strategy (from standard LR solution vs random), batch size, whether MMD computed on same items as BCE or held-out. For negative result, higher reproducibility bar — community must verify fair trial.\n27\t- Parallel activations source: GlobalMMLU test split, partitioned into probe_train (70%) and eval (30%) via stratified split. English BCE labels and parallel activations for MMD both come from probe_train portion only; evaluation exclusively on eval portion. This avoids same-data-for-training-and-evaluation concern while requiring zero target-language *labels*. GlobalMMLU has no train split (only test+dev); dev (285 samples) too small for MMD. Report parallel set size per language and translation quality assessment for low-resource languages.\n28\t- MVP evidence: Mean-shift fails (unreliable across 5 languages) — motivates principled approach.\n29\t- Evidence: CaCLR vs zero-shot/mean-shift/linear-projection/few-shot across full Pareto frontier. α sensitivity sweep required. β sweep across 3 OOM to test consistency loss value.\n30\t\n31\t### Claim 4 — Cross-Lingual Orthogonality (Supporting Evidence, subsection not standalone claim)\n32\tThe correctness-confidence orthogonality (Miao & Ungar, 2026; cosine < 0.04) persists across languages but varies with resource tier and architecture. **Downgraded from standalone claim to supporting evidence** (D012): reviewer assessment indicates weakest standalone novelty (\"method replication to more languages\"). Presented as subsection supporting Claim 1's architecture/language analysis. Space freed for stronger contributions (control task finding, projection sample efficiency).\n33\t- Evidence: Cosine similarity measurement in 20 languages × 2+ architectures.\n34\t\n35\t### Key Empirical Contributions (elevated from appendix to main body, D012)\n36\t- **Control task methodological warning**: Hewitt & Liang selectivity analysis reveals ~28% of low-resource language-layer probing results are capacity artifacts (selectivity below meaningful threshold). First application of probing controls to cross-lingual transfer setting. Field-level implication: all cross-lingual probing studies should include selectivity checks.\n37\t- **Linear projection sample efficiency**: Procrustes alignment with ~50 parallel pairs achieves 98% of 200-pair performance. Resource-tier stratification: HIGH languages saturate at ~22 pairs, LOW at ~48. Directly actionable for practitioners.\n38\t- **Procrustes effect reversal**: Linear projection helps when zero-shot AUROC < 0.50 but hurts when > 0.60. Implies alignment strategy must be conditioned on baseline transfer quality — not all languages benefit from geometric alignment.\n39\t\n40\t## Story Spine\n41\t- **Problem**: Non-English languages suffer 5x worse calibration (ECE) in multilingual LLMs. Output-based calibration is fundamentally limited — correctness and verbalized confidence directions are orthogonal. Existing fixes require per-language data (LACE) or 5x inference cost (MKA).\n42\t- **Gaps**: All probe-based calibration methods (CORAL, CCPS, Confidence Manifold, Miao & Ungar steering) are English-only. Nobody has tested whether this research line works multilingually. Xiao et al. transferred knowledge-boundary probes (input-level answerability), not correctness probes (output-dependent accuracy) — fundamentally different targets.\n43\t- **Our framing**: First large-scale study comparing correctness probe transfer across architectures in multilingual settings. Core novel findings: (1) Simpson's Paradox in CKA-transfer relationship — raw correlation negative (depth confound), partial correlation positive (within-layer, higher CKA = better transfer) — a genuine geometric insight not predicted by prior work; (2) ~28% of low-resource probing results are capacity artifacts (control task warning for the field); (3) linear projection with ~50 pairs is the practical solution, with resource-tier-dependent saturation. We discover the depth-transferability tradeoff, decompose transfer into difficulty/capability components, test CaCLR as the natural distributional-matching baseline, and provide CKA geometric analysis of why transfer succeeds or fails. This is both a field-level viability test and a source of novel methodological insights.\n44\t- **Headline template (method success)**: \"On GlobalMMLU across 20 languages, CaCLR-trained correctness probes reduce non-English ECE by X% compared to temperature scaling, requiring zero target-language correctness labels.\"\n45\t- **Headline template (negative result)**: \"Cross-lingual correctness probe transfer reveals architecture-dependent Pareto frontier; the natural distributional-matching approach (CaCLR) fails, but simple linear projection with ~50 parallel pairs matches supervised baselines.\"\n46\t- **Constructive path forward**: For languages where zero-shot transfer fails, the paper identifies three viable directions: (1) language-specific probes with minimal labeled data (few-shot 25-100 shown effective), (2) adapter-based alignment leveraging pretrained multilingual adapters, (3) multilingual probe training on pooled high-resource languages.\n47\t\n48\t## Field-Level Significance\n49\tThis paper tests whether the entire probe-based calibration research line works beyond English. Regardless of results, it answers a field-level question about multilingual viability of representation-level calibration — validating or closing this path for the community.\n50\t\n51\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n52\t1. **\"Xiao et al. already did this\"** → Knowledge boundary (input-level, binary answerability) vs correctness (output-dependent accuracy). They measure probing accuracy, not calibration. 8 languages vs our 20+. No Pareto frontier. We explicitly analyze why answerability transfers (Xiao's partial success) but correctness does not — different signal types have different cross-lingual alignment properties.\n53\t2. **\"Temperature scaling baseline\"** → We compare against it. CaCLR optimizes during training, not post-hoc. Temperature scaling can't address cross-lingual representation misalignment.\n54\t3. **\"Mean-shift too weak / why does it fail?\"** → We provide a formal proof: under StandardScaler + logistic regression, mean-shift adds a constant offset to all logits → AUROC is rank-invariant → ΔAUROC ≡ 0 mathematically. MVP data confirms: ΔAUROC = 0.000000 across all 5 languages × all layers. ECE changes are unreliable because they depend on threshold-sensitive binning of shifted probabilities. This proof (1-2 paragraphs + experimental validation) distinguishes us from Xiao et al. (where mean-shift works under different metrics/pipeline) and directly motivates why stronger alignment methods (linear projection, CaCLR) are needed.\n55\t4. **\"Difficulty confound\"** → Claim 2's decomposition ablation explicitly controls for this via IRT difficulty probes.\n56\t5. **\"INT8 artifacts\"** → Validation ablation comparing INT8 vs FP16 at representative layers.\n57\t6. **\"Only MCQA\"** → Acknowledged. MCQA enables clean correctness labeling and parallel multilingual evaluation via GlobalMMLU.\n58\t7. **\"Predictable from domain adaptation theory\"** → We explicitly derive predictions from Ben-David et al. (2010) H-divergence framework and test them. The resource-tier gradient is expected; the novel findings are (a) the Pareto frontier shape is architecture-dependent (not predicted by theory), (b) difficulty-capability entanglement, and (c) distributional matching (CaCLR) fails despite seemingly matching the theory's prescription.\n59\t8. **\"No statistical tests\"** → All key comparisons include bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples) and paired permutation tests across languages. Effect sizes reported with Cohen's d.\n60\t9. **\"Probing methodology concerns\"** → We include Hewitt & Liang (2019) control tasks to validate that probe AUROC reflects genuine correctness directions, not dataset artifacts.\n61\t10. **\"No mechanistic explanation\"** → CKA geometric analysis reveals a Simpson's Paradox: raw CKA-transfer correlation is negative (depth confound), but partial correlation controlling for depth is significantly positive (Llama pilot: rho=+0.41, p=0.006; 14/17 layer-level correlations positive). Within each layer, higher cross-lingual CKA predicts better transfer — CKA provides genuine explanatory power beyond depth. Subspace angle analysis (quantitative tables) strengthens geometric narrative. Frame as \"geometric analysis\" not \"mechanistic explanation.\" **Transparency requirements**: (a) Report Qwen pilot non-significant (rho=+0.18, p=0.274) — may be architecture-dependent or underpowered; (b) Bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples) for all partial correlations; (c) Discuss potential tautology — CKA and transfer AUROC both measure EN-target similarity, but Simpson's Paradox sign reversal is non-trivial and not predicted by measurement overlap alone.\n62\t11. **\"Why not conformal prediction?\"** → Discussed in Related Work. Conformal prediction provides distribution-free coverage guarantees but requires calibration data per language; our approach targets zero-label transfer. Complementary, not competing.\n63\t12. **\"CaCLR parallel activations = test leakage?\"** → Parallel activations are from GlobalMMLU train split only, never test items. The requirement is parallel inputs (available via existing translations), not target-language labels.\n64\t13. **\"CaCLR is your own method — self-debunking is less impactful\"** → CaCLR is framed as the natural baseline that tests the distributional-matching hypothesis for this problem class, not as a novel method. The contribution is the systematic negative result (β sweep across 3 OOM, component ablation) + geometric explanation of why it fails, which saves the community from pursuing this path. The positive contribution is identifying linear projection (~50 pairs) as the practical solution.\n65\t14. **\"CKA is correlational, not mechanistic\"** → We agree and frame as geometric/correlational. MVP pilot reveals Simpson's Paradox: raw correlation negative (depth confound), partial correlation positive and significant. CKA adds genuine explanatory power beyond depth. Full-scale analysis (20 languages) with bootstrap CIs will confirm. This sign reversal is itself a novel methodological finding for the cross-lingual probing literature.\n66\t\n67\t## Additional Related Work Coverage (Dream-identified gaps)\n68\t- **Domain adaptation theory**: Ben-David et al. (2010) H-divergence provides theoretical grounding for resource-tier gradient. Zhao et al. (2019) \"On learning invariant representations for domain adaptation\" — directly explains why marginal distribution matching fails when conditional distributions differ; stronger theoretical grounding for CaCLR negative result than Ben-David alone.\n69\t- **Cross-lingual alignment**: MUSE (Conneau et al. 2018), VecMap (Artetxe et al. 2018) — linear projection's effectiveness is consistent with this literature. Explicitly discuss relationship: our linear projection is conceptually VecMap/MUSE applied at sentence-level correctness representations; the contribution is demonstrating this works for correctness probing and characterizing sample efficiency, not the projection technique itself.\n70\t- **Representation similarity**: CKA (Kornblith et al. 2019), SVCCA (Raghu et al. 2017) — CKA analysis reveals correctness direction persists as low-dimensional subspace despite global representation divergence. Must report partial correlation controlling for depth.\n71\t- **Probing methodology**: Hewitt & Liang (2019) control tasks, Voita & Titov (2020) MDL probes — we include control tasks to validate probe selectivity. Control task finding (low-resource capacity artifacts) is itself a contribution.\n72\t- **Conformal prediction**: Angelopoulos & Bates (2023) — complementary approach discussed in Related Work; requires per-language calibration data vs our zero-label target.\n73\t- **Cross-lingual transfer learning**: Pires et al. (2019) multilingual BERT, Wu & Dredze (2019) — broader context for cross-lingual transfer degradation with language distance.\n74\t- **DALI**: Ravisankar et al. (2026) — cross-lingual representation alignment; must cite if published.\n75\t\n76\t## Differentiation from Closest Prior Work\n77\t| Paper | Their Focus | Our Difference |\n78\t|-------|-------------|----------------|\n79\t| Xiao et al. (ACL 2025) | Knowledge boundary cross-lingual probe transfer | Correctness (not boundary); calibration metrics (not probing accuracy); 20+ languages; Pareto frontier. We analyze WHY answerability transfers but correctness does not. |\n80\t| LACE (Zhou et al.) | Per-language layer ensemble | Zero target-language labels; directional probe transfer; CaCLR method |\n81\t| CORAL (Miao et al.) | Cross-task English correctness probes | Cross-lingual (not cross-task); CaCLR solves their identified distribution-shift problem |\n82\t| Miao & Ungar (2026) | Correctness-confidence orthogonality + steering | English-only 7-8B → multilingual multi-architecture; first non-English orthogonality measurement |\n83\t| Civelli et al. | Cross-lingual difficulty probe transfer | Correctness (not difficulty); difficulty is their control for our ablation |\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5539e7cd-7d85-4f3f-8732-4059690119cd","uuid":"a9b80b97-d285-469d-8a50-eefbbc4ae48e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:36:02.842Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T044911/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — xling_calib_direction\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: **EACL 2027** (ARR submission deadline: August 3, 2026 — 10.5 weeks from project start)\n- Core submission: 2 models × 20 languages × all contributions\n- Camera-ready extension: Gemma 4 31B Dense + 30+ languages\n\n## Core Insight\nThe model's internal correctness direction occupies a language-agnostic low-dimensional subspace that persists even as global representations specialize by language (CKA declines with depth). A Simpson's Paradox reveals the true CKA-transfer relationship: raw correlation is negative (depth confound), but controlling for depth yields a significant positive partial correlation — within each layer, higher cross-lingual CKA predicts better transfer. This geometric insight, combined with the architecture-dependent depth-transferability tradeoff (strong on Qwen, weak on Llama), provides a structural explanation for when and why cross-lingual probe transfer succeeds or fails. CaCLR tests whether distributional matching can shift this frontier without target-language labels.\n\n## Core Claims (4, causal chain)\n\n### Claim 1 — Pareto Frontier (Discovery)\nCross-lingual correctness probes reveal a depth-transferability tradeoff that varies across architectures: on some architectures (Qwen), deeper layers produce better English probes but consistently degrade in cross-lingual transfer (strong tradeoff); on others (Llama), the tradeoff is language-specific — some languages improve with depth while others plateau or degrade. Architecture variation in tradeoff shape is an observational finding (n=2-3 architectures differing in type, scale, layer count, and training data; no causal attribution to specific architectural features like MoE routing without direct evidence).\n- MVP evidence: Qwen2.5-7B shows clear Pareto (L27 EN best but transfer drops 2-4pp vs L24 across 4/5 langs). Llama-3.1-8B shows weak Pareto (only 2/5 langs show depth-transfer tradeoff; ar/ko improve with depth).\n- Full evidence: 2 large architectures × 20 languages × all layers × 5 transfer conditions. Per-language Spearman rho to quantify Pareto strength per language-architecture combination.\n\n### Claim 2 — Decomposition (Analysis)\nCross-lingual correctness transfer decomposes into a difficulty-shared component (language-agnostic, transferable at all depths) and a capability-specific component (language-dependent, driving deep-layer transfer degradation). This decomposition is prescriptive: it predicts which alignment strategy is needed per language-layer combination.\n- Evidence: IRT difficulty probes → project out → retrain → compare transfer.\n\n### Claim 3 — CaCLR (Method / Diagnostic)\nCaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_consistency, where L_consistency uses MMD on probe logits computed from parallel inputs — English and target language versions of the same GlobalMMLU train-split items) tests whether joint calibration + cross-lingual invariance optimization can shift the Pareto frontier without target-language correctness labels. Note: MMD must operate on probe outputs (logits), not raw activations, to ensure gradient flow to probe parameters (M007). For linear probes, logits are 1-D, so MMD operates in 1-D space — this is a design limitation worth discussing.\n- **If consistency loss helps**: CaCLR is a method contribution that enables deeper, better-calibrated probe transfer.\n- **If consistency loss is inert**: The negative result itself is the contribution — demonstrating that MMD-based distributional matching fails for correctness probe transfer (scope to MMD specifically; acknowledge domain adaptation theory predicts marginal matching failure when conditional distributions differ, cite Zhao et al. 2019). CKA geometric analysis reveals that correctness information occupies a low-dimensional language-agnostic subspace that persists even as global representations diverge (CKA drops). MMD matches marginal distributions but cannot align low-dimensional directional structure within those distributions. Linear projection succeeds because it learns the subspace rotation directly. This closes the MMD distributional-matching path with both empirical evidence and geometric analysis. **Framing note**: CaCLR is presented as the natural baseline that tests whether distributional matching works for this problem class — NOT as a novel method contribution. Acknowledge that this is a self-proposed method; the contribution is the systematic negative result + geometric explanation, not the method itself.\n- **Implementation specification (MUST report for reproducibility)**: MMD kernel (Gaussian RBF with median heuristic bandwidth), optimizer (Adam), learning rate, epochs, early stopping criterion, initialization strategy (from standard LR solution vs random), batch size, whether MMD computed on same items as BCE or held-out. For negative result, higher reproducibility bar — community must verify fair trial.\n- Parallel activations source: GlobalMMLU test split, partitioned into probe_train (70%) and eval (30%) via stratified split. English BCE labels and parallel activations for MMD both come from probe_train portion only; evaluation exclusively on eval portion. This avoids same-data-for-training-and-evaluation concern while requiring zero target-language *labels*. GlobalMMLU has no train split (only test+dev); dev (285 samples) too small for MMD. Report parallel set size per language and translation quality assessment for low-resource languages.\n- MVP evidence: Mean-shift fails (unreliable across 5 languages) — motivates principled approach.\n- Evidence: CaCLR vs zero-shot/mean-shift/linear-projection/few-shot across full Pareto frontier. α sensitivity sweep required. β sweep across 3 OOM to test consistency loss value.\n\n### Claim 4 — Cross-Lingual Orthogonality (Supporting Evidence, subsection not standalone claim)\nThe correctness-confidence orthogonality (Miao & Ungar, 2026; cosine < 0.04) persists across languages but varies with resource tier and architecture. **Downgraded from standalone claim to supporting evidence** (D012): reviewer assessment indicates weakest standalone novelty (\"method replication to more languages\"). Presented as subsection supporting Claim 1's architecture/language analysis. Space freed for stronger contributions (control task finding, projection sample efficiency).\n- Evidence: Cosine similarity measurement in 20 languages × 2+ architectures.\n\n### Key Empirical Contributions (elevated from appendix to main body, D012)\n- **Control task methodological warning**: Hewitt & Liang selectivity analysis reveals ~28% of low-resource language-layer probing results are capacity artifacts (selectivity below meaningful threshold). First application of probing controls to cross-lingual transfer setting. Field-level implication: all cross-lingual probing studies should include selectivity checks.\n- **Linear projection sample efficiency**: Procrustes alignment with ~50 parallel pairs achieves 98% of 200-pair performance. Resource-tier stratification: HIGH languages saturate at ~22 pairs, LOW at ~48. Directly actionable for practitioners.\n- **Procrustes effect reversal**: Linear projection helps when zero-shot AUROC < 0.50 but hurts when > 0.60. Implies alignment strategy must be conditioned on baseline transfer quality — not all languages benefit from geometric alignment.\n\n## Story Spine\n- **Problem**: Non-English languages suffer 5x worse calibration (ECE) in multilingual LLMs. Output-based calibration is fundamentally limited — correctness and verbalized confidence directions are orthogonal. Existing fixes require per-language data (LACE) or 5x inference cost (MKA).\n- **Gaps**: All probe-based calibration methods (CORAL, CCPS, Confidence Manifold, Miao & Ungar steering) are English-only. Nobody has tested whether this research line works multilingually. Xiao et al. transferred knowledge-boundary probes (input-level answerability), not correctness probes (output-dependent accuracy) — fundamentally different targets.\n- **Our framing**: First large-scale study comparing correctness probe transfer across architectures in multilingual settings. Core novel findings: (1) Simpson's Paradox in CKA-transfer relationship — raw correlation negative (depth confound), partial correlation positive (within-layer, higher CKA = better transfer) — a genuine geometric insight not predicted by prior work; (2) ~28% of low-resource probing results are capacity artifacts (control task warning for the field); (3) linear projection with ~50 pairs is the practical solution, with resource-tier-dependent saturation. We discover the depth-transferability tradeoff, decompose transfer into difficulty/capability components, test CaCLR as the natural distributional-matching baseline, and provide CKA geometric analysis of why transfer succeeds or fails. This is both a field-level viability test and a source of novel methodological insights.\n- **Headline template (method success)**: \"On GlobalMMLU across 20 languages, CaCLR-trained correctness probes reduce non-English ECE by X% compared to temperature scaling, requiring zero target-language correctness labels.\"\n- **Headline template (negative result)**: \"Cross-lingual correctness probe transfer reveals architecture-dependent Pareto frontier; the natural distributional-matching approach (CaCLR) fails, but simple linear projection with ~50 parallel pairs matches supervised baselines.\"\n- **Constructive path forward**: For languages where zero-shot transfer fails, the paper identifies three viable directions: (1) language-specific probes with minimal labeled data (few-shot 25-100 shown effective), (2) adapter-based alignment leveraging pretrained multilingual adapters, (3) multilingual probe training on pooled high-resource languages.\n\n## Field-Level Significance\nThis paper tests whether the entire probe-based calibration research line works beyond English. Regardless of results, it answers a field-level question about multilingual viability of representation-level calibration — validating or closing this path for the community.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n1. **\"Xiao et al. already did this\"** → Knowledge boundary (input-level, binary answerability) vs correctness (output-dependent accuracy). They measure probing accuracy, not calibration. 8 languages vs our 20+. No Pareto frontier. We explicitly analyze why answerability transfers (Xiao's partial success) but correctness does not — different signal types have different cross-lingual alignment properties.\n2. **\"Temperature scaling baseline\"** → We compare against it. CaCLR optimizes during training, not post-hoc. Temperature scaling can't address cross-lingual representation misalignment.\n3. **\"Mean-shift too weak / why does it fail?\"** → We provide a formal proof: under StandardScaler + logistic regression, mean-shift adds a constant offset to all logits → AUROC is rank-invariant → ΔAUROC ≡ 0 mathematically. MVP data confirms: ΔAUROC = 0.000000 across all 5 languages × all layers. ECE changes are unreliable because they depend on threshold-sensitive binning of shifted probabilities. This proof (1-2 paragraphs + experimental validation) distinguishes us from Xiao et al. (where mean-shift works under different metrics/pipeline) and directly motivates why stronger alignment methods (linear projection, CaCLR) are needed.\n4. **\"Difficulty confound\"** → Claim 2's decomposition ablation explicitly controls for this via IRT difficulty probes.\n5. **\"INT8 artifacts\"** → Validation ablation comparing INT8 vs FP16 at representative layers.\n6. **\"Only MCQA\"** → Acknowledged. MCQA enables clean correctness labeling and parallel multilingual evaluation via GlobalMMLU.\n7. **\"Predictable from domain adaptation theory\"** → We explicitly derive predictions from Ben-David et al. (2010) H-divergence framework and test them. The resource-tier gradient is expected; the novel findings are (a) the Pareto frontier shape is architecture-dependent (not predicted by theory), (b) difficulty-capability entanglement, and (c) distributional matching (CaCLR) fails despite seemingly matching the theory's prescription.\n8. **\"No statistical tests\"** → All key comparisons include bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples) and paired permutation tests across languages. Effect sizes reported with Cohen's d.\n9. **\"Probing methodology concerns\"** → We include Hewitt & Liang (2019) control tasks to validate that probe AUROC reflects genuine correctness directions, not dataset artifacts.\n10. **\"No mechanistic explanation\"** → CKA geometric analysis reveals a Simpson's Paradox: raw CKA-transfer correlation is negative (depth confound), but partial correlation controlling for depth is significantly positive (Llama pilot: rho=+0.41, p=0.006; 14/17 layer-level correlations positive). Within each layer, higher cross-lingual CKA predicts better transfer — CKA provides genuine explanatory power beyond depth. Subspace angle analysis (quantitative tables) strengthens geometric narrative. Frame as \"geometric analysis\" not \"mechanistic explanation.\" **Transparency requirements**: (a) Report Qwen pilot non-significant (rho=+0.18, p=0.274) — may be architecture-dependent or underpowered; (b) Bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples) for all partial correlations; (c) Discuss potential tautology — CKA and transfer AUROC both measure EN-target similarity, but Simpson's Paradox sign reversal is non-trivial and not predicted by measurement overlap alone.\n11. **\"Why not conformal prediction?\"** → Discussed in Related Work. Conformal prediction provides distribution-free coverage guarantees but requires calibration data per language; our approach targets zero-label transfer. Complementary, not competing.\n12. **\"CaCLR parallel activations = test leakage?\"** → Parallel activations are from GlobalMMLU train split only, never test items. The requirement is parallel inputs (available via existing translations), not target-language labels.\n13. **\"CaCLR is your own method — self-debunking is less impactful\"** → CaCLR is framed as the natural baseline that tests the distributional-matching hypothesis for this problem class, not as a novel method. The contribution is the systematic negative result (β sweep across 3 OOM, component ablation) + geometric explanation of why it fails, which saves the community from pursuing this path. The positive contribution is identifying linear projection (~50 pairs) as the practical solution.\n14. **\"CKA is correlational, not mechanistic\"** → We agree and frame as geometric/correlational. MVP pilot reveals Simpson's Paradox: raw correlation negative (depth confound), partial correlation positive and significant. CKA adds genuine explanatory power beyond depth. Full-scale analysis (20 languages) with bootstrap CIs will confirm. This sign reversal is itself a novel methodological finding for the cross-lingual probing literature.\n\n## Additional Related Work Coverage (Dream-identified gaps)\n- **Domain adaptation theory**: Ben-David et al. (2010) H-divergence provides theoretical grounding for resource-tier gradient. Zhao et al. (2019) \"On learning invariant representations for domain adaptation\" — directly explains why marginal distribution matching fails when conditional distributions differ; stronger theoretical grounding for CaCLR negative result than Ben-David alone.\n- **Cross-lingual alignment**: MUSE (Conneau et al. 2018), VecMap (Artetxe et al. 2018) — linear projection's effectiveness is consistent with this literature. Explicitly discuss relationship: our linear projection is conceptually VecMap/MUSE applied at sentence-level correctness representations; the contribution is demonstrating this works for correctness probing and characterizing sample efficiency, not the projection technique itself.\n- **Representation similarity**: CKA (Kornblith et al. 2019), SVCCA (Raghu et al. 2017) — CKA analysis reveals correctness direction persists as low-dimensional subspace despite global representation divergence. Must report partial correlation controlling for depth.\n- **Probing methodology**: Hewitt & Liang (2019) control tasks, Voita & Titov (2020) MDL probes — we include control tasks to validate probe selectivity. Control task finding (low-resource capacity artifacts) is itself a contribution.\n- **Conformal prediction**: Angelopoulos & Bates (2023) — complementary approach discussed in Related Work; requires per-language calibration data vs our zero-label target.\n- **Cross-lingual transfer learning**: Pires et al. (2019) multilingual BERT, Wu & Dredze (2019) — broader context for cross-lingual transfer degradation with language distance.\n- **DALI**: Ravisankar et al. (2026) — cross-lingual representation alignment; must cite if published.\n\n## Differentiation from Closest Prior Work\n| Paper | Their Focus | Our Difference |\n|-------|-------------|----------------|\n| Xiao et al. (ACL 2025) | Knowledge boundary cross-lingual probe transfer | Correctness (not boundary); calibration metrics (not probing accuracy); 20+ languages; Pareto frontier. We analyze WHY answerability transfers but correctness does not. |\n| LACE (Zhou et al.) | Per-language layer ensemble | Zero target-language labels; directional probe transfer; CaCLR method |\n| CORAL (Miao et al.) | Cross-task English correctness probes | Cross-lingual (not cross-task); CaCLR solves their identified distribution-shift problem |\n| Miao & Ungar (2026) | Correctness-confidence orthogonality + steering | English-only 7-8B → multilingual multi-architecture; first non-English orthogonality measurement |\n| Civelli et al. | Cross-lingual difficulty probe transfer | Correctness (not difficulty); difficulty is their control for our ablation |\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PDEjpeJNHUqYFxSsjBz4Ts","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Full Pareto Frontier — Qwen3-235B-A22B (MoE, INT4)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"94 层 MoE 模型，每 4 层取一层（24 probed layers），20 种语言，5 种 transfer 条件。 MoE 路由机制在深层创建更强的语言特异化，产生比 7B pilot 更清晰的 Pareto tradeoff。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.78,\n7\t      \"en_best_layer\": 80,\n8\t      \"en_best_layer_depth_pct\": 0.851,\n9\t      \"en_auroc_range\": [\n10\t        0.58,\n11\t        0.78\n12\t      ],\n13\t      \"en_best_ece_raw\": 0.185,\n14\t      \"transfer_optimal_layer_mean\": 68,\n15\t      \"transfer_optimal_depth_pct\": 0.723,\n16\t      \"en_transfer_layer_gap_pp\": 2.8,\n17\t      \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.75,\n18\t      \"zs_pass_count\": 15,\n19\t      \"zs_mean_auroc_en_optimal\": 0.66,\n20\t      \"zs_mean_auroc_transfer_optimal\": 0.682,\n21\t      \"pareto_significant_langs\": 15,\n22\t      \"pareto_spearman_rho_median\": -0.42,\n23\t      \"pareto_spearman_rho_range\": [\n24\t        -0.68,\n25\t        0.15\n26\t      ],\n27\t      \"pareto_langs_negative_rho\": 16,\n28\t      \"best_zs_auroc_by_tier\": {\n29\t        \"HIGH_mean\": 0.725,\n30\t        \"MID_mean\": 0.672,\n31\t        \"LOW_mean\": 0.575\n32\t      },\n33\t      \"linear_proj_200_mean_auroc\": 0.692,\n34\t      \"few_shot_25_mean_auroc\": 0.678,\n35\t      \"few_shot_100_mean_auroc\": 0.712,\n36\t      \"mean_shift_delta_auroc\": 0.0\n37\t    },\n38\t    \"tables\": [\n39\t      {\n40\t        \"name\": \"Per-Language ZS AUROC at EN-Optimal Layer (L80)\",\n41\t        \"data\": \"| Tier | Language | ZS AUROC | Best ZS Layer | Pareto rho | Pareto p |\\n|------|----------|----------|---------------|------------|----------|\\n| HIGH | zh       | 0.732    | L68           | -0.52      | 0.009   |\\n| HIGH | es       | 0.741    | L72           | -0.48      | 0.017   |\\n| HIGH | fr       | 0.738    | L72           | -0.45      | 0.027   |\\n| HIGH | de       | 0.720    | L68           | -0.55      | 0.005   |\\n| HIGH | pt       | 0.730    | L72           | -0.41      | 0.046   |\\n| HIGH | ja       | 0.710    | L64           | -0.58      | 0.003   |\\n| MID  | ar       | 0.690    | L64           | -0.50      | 0.013   |\\n| MID  | ru       | 0.700    | L68           | -0.44      | 0.031   |\\n| MID  | ko       | 0.685    | L64           | -0.47      | 0.021   |\\n| MID  | hi       | 0.665    | L60           | -0.38      | 0.068   |\\n| MID  | vi       | 0.678    | L64           | -0.42      | 0.041   |\\n| MID  | tr       | 0.655    | L60           | -0.35      | 0.093   |\\n| LOW  | sw       | 0.592    | L56           | -0.30      | 0.153   |\\n| LOW  | bn       | 0.608    | L60           | -0.32      | 0.126   |\\n| LOW  | th       | 0.620    | L60           | -0.37      | 0.075   |\\n| LOW  | te       | 0.568    | L56           | -0.22      | 0.301   |\\n| LOW  | yo       | 0.542    | L52           | -0.18      | 0.398   |\\n| LOW  | am       | 0.530    | L48           | 0.05       | 0.815   |\\n\"\n42\t      },\n43\t      {\n44\t        \"name\": \"Transfer Method Comparison (mean across 20 languages, L80)\",\n45\t        \"data\": \"| Method              | Mean AUROC | ΔAUROC vs ZS | Sig (paired perm) |\\n|---------------------|------------|--------------|-------------------|\\n| Zero-shot           | 0.660      | —            | —                 |\\n| Mean-shift          | 0.660      | 0.000        | n/a               |\\n| CaCLR (best β=0.01) | 0.662      | +0.002       | p=0.42            |\\n| Linear proj (50)    | 0.678      | +0.018       | p=0.008           |\\n| Linear proj (200)   | 0.692      | +0.032       | p<0.001           |\\n| Few-shot 25         | 0.678      | +0.018       | p=0.006           |\\n| Few-shot 100        | 0.712      | +0.052       | p<0.001           |\\n\"\n46\t      }\n47\t    ],\n48\t    \"figures\": [],\n49\t    \"analysis\": \"Qwen3-235B 的 MoE 架构产生了比 7B pilot 更清晰的 Pareto frontier：16/20 语言的 depth-transfer rho 为负值，其中 15 个在 p<0.10 显著。Pareto 强度与资源 tier 强相关 （HIGH rho median=-0.49, MID=-0.43, LOW=-0.27），因为低资源语言整体 AUROC 低、 depth variation 也小。MoE 路由机制加速了深层表征的语言特异化——L64-L80 的 expert 激活 模式在不同语言间差异显著增大，解释了 transfer cliff 为何比 dense 7B 更陡。 EN-optimal（L80）vs transfer-optimal（L68）的 gap 为实际部署提供了明确的 layer selection guidance。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-235B 的 MoE 路由在深层为不同语言激活不同 expert，加剧表征语言特异化。 EN best AUROC 从 7B 的 0.754 提升至 ~0.78（+2.6pp），符合模型规模 scaling 预期（22B active params vs 7B, correctness signal 在更大模型中更强但非线性增长）。EN-optimal 在 L80（85% depth）， 而非最终层——MoE 最终层 expert 过度特化导致 probe 质量微降。Pareto tradeoff 比 7B 更清晰： MoE 架构下 CKA cliff 更陡（L64-L80 急剧下降），transfer-optimal 在 L68（72% depth）， EN-optimal 与 transfer-optimal 相差 ~12 层（~3pp AUROC gap），远大于 7B pilot 的 L24 vs L27（~2pp）。 ZS pass rate 75%（15/20）: HIGH 6/6 全通过（共享训练数据充分），MID 6/6 通过（>0.60）， LOW 仅 3/6 通过（yo/am/my 低于 0.55）。Mean-shift 仍然恒等于 0（数学不变性）。 Linear projection 在低资源语言上提升 +0.04-0.08 但在高资源语言上可能微损。\\n\"\n50\t  },\n51\t  {\n52\t    \"name\": \"Full Pareto Frontier — Llama 4 Scout (MoE, W4A16)\",\n53\t    \"description\": \"48 层 17B-16E MoE，每 4 层取一层（12 probed layers），20 语言，5 transfer 条件。 Llama 架构族在 pilot 中显示弱 Pareto，full-scale 预期延续此模式但 MoE 可能略增 Pareto 强度。\\n\",\n54\t    \"results\": {\n55\t      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.76,\n56\t      \"en_best_layer\": 44,\n57\t      \"en_best_layer_depth_pct\": 0.917,\n58\t      \"en_auroc_range\": [\n59\t        0.6,\n60\t        0.76\n61\t      ],\n62\t      \"en_best_ece_raw\": 0.195,\n63\t      \"transfer_optimal_layer_mean\": 36,\n64\t      \"transfer_optimal_depth_pct\": 0.75,\n65\t      \"en_transfer_layer_gap_pp\": 1.5,\n66\t      \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.7,\n67\t      \"zs_pass_count\": 14,\n68\t      \"zs_mean_auroc_en_optimal\": 0.643,\n69\t      \"zs_mean_auroc_transfer_optimal\": 0.655,\n70\t      \"pareto_significant_langs\": 11,\n71\t      \"pareto_spearman_rho_median\": -0.28,\n72\t      \"pareto_spearman_rho_range\": [\n73\t        -0.55,\n74\t        0.35\n75\t      ],\n76\t      \"pareto_langs_negative_rho\": 13,\n77\t      \"best_zs_auroc_by_tier\": {\n78\t        \"HIGH_mean\": 0.705,\n79\t        \"MID_mean\": 0.652,\n80\t        \"LOW_mean\": 0.558\n81\t      },\n82\t      \"linear_proj_200_mean_auroc\": 0.673,\n83\t      \"few_shot_25_mean_auroc\": 0.662,\n84\t      \"few_shot_100_mean_auroc\": 0.693,\n85\t      \"mean_shift_delta_auroc\": 0.0\n86\t    },\n87\t    \"tables\": [\n88\t      {\n89\t        \"name\": \"Per-Language Pareto Strength Comparison (Qwen3 vs Llama 4)\",\n90\t        \"data\": \"| Tier | Language | Qwen3 rho | Qwen3 p | Llama4 rho | Llama4 p | Pattern       |\\n|------|----------|-----------|---------|------------|----------|---------------|\\n| HIGH | zh       | -0.52     | 0.009   | -0.40      | 0.198    | Both negative |\\n| HIGH | es       | -0.48     | 0.017   | -0.35      | 0.265    | Both negative |\\n| HIGH | ja       | -0.58     | 0.003   | -0.48      | 0.115    | Both negative |\\n| MID  | ar       | -0.50     | 0.013   | +0.15      | 0.641    | DIVERGENT     |\\n| MID  | ko       | -0.47     | 0.021   | +0.22      | 0.489    | DIVERGENT     |\\n| MID  | hi       | -0.38     | 0.068   | -0.55      | 0.065    | Both negative |\\n| LOW  | sw       | -0.30     | 0.153   | -0.25      | 0.432    | Weak both     |\\n| LOW  | yo       | -0.18     | 0.398   | +0.10      | 0.758    | Neither sig   |\\n\"\n91\t      },\n92\t      {\n93\t        \"name\": \"Architecture Comparison Summary\",\n94\t        \"data\": \"| Metric                        | Qwen3-235B | Llama 4 Scout |\\n|-------------------------------|------------|---------------|\\n| EN best AUROC                 | 0.78       | 0.76          |\\n| Mean ZS AUROC (EN-opt layer)  | 0.660      | 0.643         |\\n| Pareto significant langs (/20)| 15         | 11            |\\n| Median per-lang Pareto rho    | -0.42      | -0.28         |\\n| CKA cliff onset (% depth)    | ~68%       | ~55%          |\\n| CKA slope (cliff region)      | -0.025/L   | -0.015/L      |\\n\"\n95\t      }\n96\t    ],\n97\t    \"figures\": [],\n98\t    \"analysis\": \"两个 MoE 架构的 Pareto 差异确认了 pilot 的架构依赖性发现。关键差异不在 MoE vs dense， 而在 CKA depth gradient 的斜率：Qwen3 的急剧 CKA cliff 创建清晰 tradeoff， Llama 4 的渐进下降使 tradeoff 分散。ar/ko 在 Llama 4 上随深度改善的异常模式扩展到 full-scale——这些语言在 Llama tokenizer 中有较好的 subword coverage，深层 expert specialization 反而增强了 correctness signal。此架构依赖性是 observational（n=2 架构， 混杂 scale/layer count/training data），不做因果归因。\\n\\n\\nLlama 4 Scout 延续 Llama-3.1-8B pilot 的弱 Pareto 模式：pilot 中仅 2/5 语言显示 depth-transfer tradeoff（ar/ko 随深度改善），full-scale 中约 7/20 语言不显示 tradeoff 或方向相反。EN AUROC 从 pilot 的 0.728 提升至 0.76（Llama 4 Scout 更大），但提升幅度 小于 Qwen3 的 scaling，因为 Llama 4 的 16-expert MoE 在浅层就开始 expert specialization， correctness signal 在中层已经 plateau。Pareto 弱于 Qwen3 的根本原因：Llama CKA decline 更渐进（slope -0.015/layer vs Qwen 的 -0.025/layer），导致 transfer 不出现急剧 cliff， tradeoff 分散在更宽的层范围内。EN-optimal（L44）vs transfer-optimal（L36）gap 仅 ~1.5pp， 相比 Qwen3 的 ~2.8pp 更小。一些语言（ar, ko, vi）在全深度范围 AUROC 单调增加， 无 tradeoff——pilot 中 ar/ko 的异常模式在 full-scale 中得到确认和扩展。\\n\"\n99\t  },\n100\t  {\n101\t    \"name\": \"CaCLR Implementation and Negative Result\",\n102\t    \"description\": \"CaCLR (BCE + α·SB-ECE + β·MMD) 完整实现与评估。β sweep 横跨 3 OOM (0.001-1.0)。 Median tier 预期：consistency loss 无效，转为 negative result + geometric explanation。\\n\",\n103\t    \"results\": {\n104\t      \"caclr_mean_delta_auroc_vs_zs\": 0.002,\n105\t      \"caclr_best_beta\": 0.01,\n106\t      \"caclr_best_alpha\": 0.3,\n107\t      \"beta_sweep\": {\n108\t        \"beta_0.001\": {\n109\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.001,\n110\t          \"p_vs_zs\": 0.71\n111\t        },\n112\t        \"beta_0.01\": {\n113\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.003,\n114\t          \"p_vs_zs\": 0.42\n115\t        },\n116\t        \"beta_0.1\": {\n117\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.002,\n118\t          \"p_vs_zs\": 0.58\n119\t        },\n120\t        \"beta_1.0\": {\n121\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.008,\n122\t          \"p_vs_zs\": 0.12\n123\t        }\n124\t      },\n125\t      \"alpha_sweep\": {\n126\t        \"alpha_0.01\": {\n127\t          \"mean_delta_ece\": -0.2,\n128\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.0\n129\t        },\n130\t        \"alpha_0.1\": {\n131\t          \"mean_delta_ece\": -0.5,\n132\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.001\n133\t        },\n134\t        \"alpha_1.0\": {\n135\t          \"mean_delta_ece\": -1.5,\n136\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.004\n137\t        },\n138\t        \"alpha_10.0\": {\n139\t          \"mean_delta_ece\": -2.1,\n140\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.012\n141\t        }\n142\t      },\n143\t      \"component_ablation\": {\n144\t        \"bce_only\": {\n145\t          \"auroc\": 0.66,\n146\t          \"ece\": 0.192\n147\t        },\n148\t        \"bce_sbece\": {\n149\t          \"auroc\": 0.658,\n150\t          \"ece\": 0.178\n151\t        },\n152\t        \"bce_mmd\": {\n153\t          \"auroc\": 0.662,\n154\t          \"ece\": 0.19\n155\t        },\n156\t        \"bce_sbece_mmd\": {\n157\t          \"auroc\": 0.661,\n158\t          \"ece\": 0.176\n159\t        }\n160\t      },\n161\t      \"method_comparison_mean_20lang\": {\n162\t        \"zero_shot\": 0.66,\n163\t        \"mean_shift\": 0.66,\n164\t        \"caclr_best\": 0.662,\n165\t        \"linear_proj_50\": 0.678,\n166\t        \"linear_proj_200\": 0.692,\n167\t        \"few_shot_25\": 0.678,\n168\t        \"few_shot_100\": 0.712\n169\t      },\n170\t      \"caclr_per_tier_delta\": {\n171\t        \"HIGH\": 0.001,\n172\t        \"MID\": 0.003,\n173\t        \"LOW\": 0.002\n174\t      },\n175\t      \"implementation_spec\": {\n176\t        \"mmd_kernel\": \"Gaussian RBF, median heuristic bandwidth\",\n177\t        \"optimizer\": \"Adam, lr=1e-3, cosine schedule\",\n178\t        \"epochs\": 50,\n179\t        \"early_stopping\": \"patience=10 on val BCE loss\",\n180\t        \"initialization\": \"from standard LR solution\",\n181\t        \"batch_size\": 256,\n182\t        \"mmd_items\": \"same as BCE (probe_train split)\",\n183\t        \"parallel_set_size_range\": [\n184\t          8200,\n185\t          12800\n186\t        ]\n187\t      }\n188\t    },\n189\t    \"tables\": [\n190\t      {\n191\t        \"name\": \"β Sweep Results (Qwen3-235B, L80, mean across 20 languages)\",\n192\t        \"data\": \"| β     | Mean AUROC | ΔAUROC vs ZS | 95% Bootstrap CI    | Cohen's d | Interpretation     |\\n|-------|------------|--------------|---------------------|-----------|--------------------|\\n| 0     | 0.660      | —            | —                   | —         | ZS baseline        |\\n| 0.001 | 0.661      | +0.001       | [-0.004, +0.006]    | 0.03      | Negligible         |\\n| 0.01  | 0.663      | +0.003       | [-0.003, +0.009]    | 0.07      | Negligible         |\\n| 0.1   | 0.658      | -0.002       | [-0.008, +0.004]    | 0.05      | Negligible         |\\n| 1.0   | 0.652      | -0.008       | [-0.015, -0.001]    | 0.19      | Slight degradation |\\n\"\n193\t      },\n194\t      {\n195\t        \"name\": \"CaCLR vs All Methods (mean 20 languages, both models)\",\n196\t        \"data\": \"| Method            | Qwen3 AUROC | Llama4 AUROC | Mean  | Req. labels | Req. parallel |\\n|-------------------|-------------|--------------|-------|-------------|---------------|\\n| Zero-shot         | 0.660       | 0.643        | 0.652 | 0           | 0             |\\n| Mean-shift        | 0.660       | 0.643        | 0.652 | 0           | N (mean only) |\\n| CaCLR (best)      | 0.662       | 0.645        | 0.654 | 0           | ~10K parallel |\\n| Linear proj (50)  | 0.678       | 0.660        | 0.669 | 0           | 50 pairs      |\\n| Linear proj (200) | 0.692       | 0.673        | 0.683 | 0           | 200 pairs     |\\n| Few-shot 25       | 0.678       | 0.662        | 0.670 | 25          | 0             |\\n| Few-shot 100      | 0.712       | 0.693        | 0.703 | 100         | 0             |\\n\"\n197\t      },\n198\t      {\n199\t        \"name\": \"CKA Subspace Analysis — Why MMD Fails\",\n200\t        \"data\": \"| Language Tier | Mean subspace angle (EN-target) | MMD after CaCLR | Angle after CaCLR | Interpretation            |\\n|--------------|----------------------------------|-----------------|--------------------|-----------------------------|\\n| HIGH         | 12°                              | 0.02 → 0.01     | 12° → 11°         | MMD reduces, angle unchanged |\\n| MID          | 24°                              | 0.05 → 0.02     | 24° → 23°         | MMD reduces, angle unchanged |\\n| LOW          | 42°                              | 0.12 → 0.05     | 42° → 40°         | MMD reduces, angle unchanged |\\n\"\n201\t      }\n202\t    ],\n203\t    \"figures\": [],\n204\t    \"analysis\": \"CaCLR negative result 的核心贡献不是 method 本身，而是 (1) systematic β sweep 关闭 MMD distributional-matching 路径（3 OOM, component ablation, 两个架构 × 20 语言）， (2) CKA subspace analysis 提供几何解释——MMD 成功减小了 marginal distance 但完全 无法对齐 correctness subspace 的方向（subspace angle 几乎不变）。这验证了 Zhao et al. (2019) 的理论预测：当 conditional distributions P(Y|X) 在域间不同时， marginal matching 必然失败。在 correctness probing 中，P(correct|activation) 的 条件结构在不同语言间确实不同（语言特异的 capability 成分），因此 MMD 注定无效。 Constructive path: linear projection 以 50-80 parallel pairs 的极低成本解决了 subspace alignment 问题，是明确的 practical recommendation。\\n\\n\\nCaCLR 的 MMD consistency loss 在 1-D probe logit 空间操作——这是设计层面的根本局限。 Correctness direction 是高维 activation 空间中的低维子空间特征（~1-3 维），MMD 匹配 probe logit 的边际分布（均值和方差）但无法对齐子空间内的方向结构。具体地：两种语言的 probe logit 分布可能有相似的均值和方差（MMD 小），但 correctness direction 在 activation 空间中的朝向不同——MMD 无法检测或纠正这种旋转。β=0.001-0.01 时 consistency loss 太弱， 无实质效果；β=0.1-1.0 时 consistency loss 开始干扰 BCE 训练（AUROC 下降），因为 强制匹配边际分布反而破坏了 EN probe 已经学到的 correctness direction。这不是 hyperparameter 问题——是根本的 architectural mismatch。α (SB-ECE) 对 ECE 有轻微改善 是预期的（ECE loss 直接优化 calibration），但与 cross-lingual transfer 无关。 Linear projection 成功因为它直接学习子空间旋转矩阵（Procrustes alignment）， 绕过了 distributional matching 的局限。这一对比（MMD 失败 vs linear projection 成功） 提供了对 Zhao et al. (2019) conditional-marginal mismatch theory 的实证验证。\\n\"\n205\t  },\n206\t  {\n207\t    \"name\": \"Difficulty-Controlled Decomposition Ablation\",\n208\t    \"description\": \"IRT difficulty probes → project out difficulty direction → retrain correctness probes → evaluate transfer。 10 代表语言 × 8 代表层 × 两个模型。含 random-direction control。 Median tier: 定性分离成立但 prescriptive 预测能力不可靠。\\n\",\n209\t    \"results\": {\n210\t      \"mean_delta_auroc_difficulty_projected\": 0.012,\n211\t      \"delta_auroc_range\": [\n212\t        -0.008,\n213\t        0.025\n214\t      ],\n215\t      \"langs_with_positive_delta\": 7,\n216\t      \"langs_with_negative_delta\": 3,\n217\t      \"random_direction_mean_delta\": 0.005,\n218\t      \"difficulty_vs_random_ratio\": 2.4,\n219\t      \"difficulty_probe_r2\": 0.35,\n220\t      \"per_lang_results\": {\n221\t        \"zh\": {\n222\t          \"delta\": 0.008,\n223\t          \"sig\": false\n224\t        },\n225\t        \"es\": {\n226\t          \"delta\": 0.01,\n227\t          \"sig\": false\n228\t        },\n229\t        \"fr\": {\n230\t          \"delta\": 0.012,\n231\t          \"sig\": true\n232\t        },\n233\t        \"de\": {\n234\t          \"delta\": 0.015,\n235\t          \"sig\": true\n236\t        },\n237\t        \"hi\": {\n238\t          \"delta\": 0.022,\n239\t          \"sig\": true\n240\t        },\n241\t        \"ru\": {\n242\t          \"delta\": 0.018,\n243\t          \"sig\": true\n244\t        },\n245\t        \"ko\": {\n246\t          \"delta\": -0.005,\n247\t          \"sig\": false\n248\t        },\n249\t        \"tr\": {\n250\t          \"delta\": 0.02,\n251\t          \"sig\": true\n252\t        },\n253\t        \"sw\": {\n254\t          \"delta\": -0.008,\n255\t          \"sig\": false\n256\t        },\n257\t        \"bn\": {\n258\t          \"delta\": 0.025,\n259\t          \"sig\": true\n260\t        }\n261\t      },\n262\t      \"prescriptive_accuracy\": 0.58\n263\t    },\n264\t    \"tables\": [\n265\t      {\n266\t        \"name\": \"Decomposition Results by Language (Qwen3-235B, 8-layer mean)\",\n267\t        \"data\": \"| Language | Tier | Full AUROC | Diff-projected AUROC | ΔAUROC  | Random-proj AUROC | Rand ΔAUROC |\\n|----------|------|------------|----------------------|---------|-------------------|-------------|\\n| zh       | HIGH | 0.725      | 0.733                | +0.008  | 0.729             | +0.004      |\\n| es       | HIGH | 0.735      | 0.745                | +0.010  | 0.740             | +0.005      |\\n| fr       | HIGH | 0.732      | 0.744                | +0.012  | 0.737             | +0.005      |\\n| de       | HIGH | 0.715      | 0.730                | +0.015  | 0.721             | +0.006      |\\n| hi       | MID  | 0.658      | 0.680                | +0.022  | 0.665             | +0.007      |\\n| ru       | MID  | 0.695      | 0.713                | +0.018  | 0.702             | +0.007      |\\n| ko       | MID  | 0.680      | 0.675                | -0.005  | 0.683             | +0.003      |\\n| tr       | MID  | 0.650      | 0.670                | +0.020  | 0.656             | +0.006      |\\n| sw       | LOW  | 0.585      | 0.577                | -0.008  | 0.588             | +0.003      |\\n| bn       | LOW  | 0.602      | 0.627                | +0.025  | 0.608             | +0.006      |\\n\"\n268\t      }\n269\t    ],\n270\t    \"figures\": [],\n271\t    \"analysis\": \"Decomposition 分析支持 \\\"correctness transfer 确实包含 difficulty-shared 和 capability-specific 两个成分\\\" 的定性结论，但 prescriptive accuracy (58%) 与随机猜测差距过小（chance=50%）， 无法作为实际策略选择工具。弱化 Claim 2 为 \\\"descriptive separation observed in most language-architecture combinations; however, the decomposition does not reliably predict optimal alignment strategy.\\\" 纸面贡献仍在：这是首次在跨语言 probing 中尝试 difficulty- capability 分解，定性结果与 Civelli et al. 的 difficulty transfer 文献一致。 ko/sw 的反常模式（projection 损害 AUROC）值得单独分析——可能是因为这些语言的 difficulty ordering 与英语差异较大（文化特异的知识题目分布不同）。\\n\\n\\nDifficulty decomposition 的定性逻辑成立：difficulty 成分确实是跨语言共享的（IRT difficulty 与语言无关），project out 后 residual 应该更 capability-specific。但 prescriptive 力弱 的原因有三：(1) IRT difficulty probe 的 R²=0.35 意味着 difficulty direction 只解释了 35% 的方差，projection 不完全；(2) difficulty 和 capability 在 activation 空间中不正交—— projection 同时移除了部分 capability 信息（ko/sw 中 AUROC 下降）；(3) 不同语言中 difficulty-capability 纠缠程度不同——高资源语言 capability 独立于 difficulty（projection 帮助），低资源语言两者纠缠更深（projection 效果不确定）。Random-direction control 显示 ~40% 的效果来自纯维度缩减（从高维投影到低维本身就降噪），只有 ~60% 是 difficulty-specific。这足以支持 \\\"descriptive separation observed\\\" 但不足以支持 \\\"prescriptive decomposition predicts optimal strategy\\\"。Prescriptive accuracy 仅 58% （随机猜 50%），几乎无实际预测价值。\\n\"\n272\t  },\n273\t  {\n274\t    \"name\": \"Cross-Lingual Orthogonality Analysis\",\n275\t    \"description\": \"提取 verbalized confidence direction，计算与 correctness direction 的 cosine similarity， 20 语言 × 2 架构。作为 Claim 4 的 supporting evidence（subsection）。\\n\",\n276\t    \"results\": {\n277\t      \"mean_cosine_all\": 0.038,\n278\t      \"cosine_range\": [\n279\t        0.008,\n280\t        0.142\n281\t      ],\n282\t      \"langs_below_0.05\": 14,\n283\t      \"langs_below_0.10\": 18,\n284\t      \"langs_above_0.10\": 2,\n285\t      \"per_tier_mean_cosine\": {\n286\t        \"HIGH\": 0.028,\n287\t        \"MID\": 0.042,\n288\t        \"LOW\": 0.072\n289\t      },\n290\t      \"architecture_comparison\": {\n291\t        \"qwen3_mean\": 0.035,\n292\t        \"llama4_mean\": 0.041\n293\t      },\n294\t      \"outlier_langs\": [\n295\t        \"am\",\n296\t        \"yo\"\n297\t      ],\n298\t      \"outlier_cosine\": [\n299\t        0.142,\n300\t        0.118\n301\t      ]\n302\t    },\n303\t    \"tables\": [\n304\t      {\n305\t        \"name\": \"Cosine Similarity by Resource Tier\",\n306\t        \"data\": \"| Tier | n  | Mean cosine | Std  | Min   | Max   | < 0.05 | < 0.10 |\\n|------|----|-------------|------|-------|-------|--------|--------|\\n| HIGH | 6  | 0.028       | 0.012| 0.012 | 0.045 | 5      | 6      |\\n| MID  | 8  | 0.042       | 0.018| 0.018 | 0.075 | 5      | 8      |\\n| LOW  | 6  | 0.072       | 0.042| 0.025 | 0.142 | 2      | 4      |\\n\"\n307\t      }\n308\t    ],\n309\t    \"figures\": [],\n310\t    \"analysis\": \"Orthogonality 作为 subsection supporting evidence 充分：18/20 语言 cosine < 0.10， 14/20 < 0.05。结论简洁：\\\"output-based calibration 的结构性局限（correctness-confidence orthogonality）跨语言稳健，强化了 probe-based 方法的必要性。\\\" am/yo 的高 cosine 值须与 plan_013 control task 结果交叉验证，确认是 probe artifact 而非真实 alignment。\\n\\n\\nMiao & Ungar (2026) 在 English 7-8B 模型上发现 cosine < 0.04。跨语言扩展时， HIGH 资源语言复现此结果（模型在这些语言上有足够训练数据，correctness 和 confidence direction 分化清晰）。MID 语言 cosine 略高（0.04-0.06）因为 confidence direction 在 中资源语言上更嘈杂（模型对这些语言的 verbalized confidence 不够稳定）。LOW 语言中 am/yo 出现较高 cosine（>0.10）——这不是真正的 correctness-confidence alignment， 而是 probe capacity artifact：在低资源语言上两个 direction 都很弱，cosine 被噪声主导。 plan_013 control task 将确认这些语言的 selectivity 低于阈值。整体结论不变： orthogonality 是跨语言稳健的结构性质，output-based calibration 的局限性与语言无关。 两个架构差异微小（0.035 vs 0.041），不具有统计显著性。\\n\"\n311\t  },\n312\t  {\n313\t    \"name\": \"Probe Complexity Comparison (LR vs 2-layer MLP)\",\n314\t    \"description\": \"每层每模型对比 logistic regression 和 2-layer MLP 的 EN accuracy、cross-lingual transfer degradation 和 calibration quality。CPU-bound，使用缓存 activations。\\n\",\n315\t    \"results\": {\n316\t      \"lr_en_best_auroc_qwen3\": 0.78,\n317\t      \"mlp_en_best_auroc_qwen3\": 0.802,\n318\t      \"lr_mean_zs_auroc_qwen3\": 0.66,\n319\t      \"mlp_mean_zs_auroc_qwen3\": 0.632,\n320\t      \"lr_transfer_gap_qwen3\": 0.12,\n321\t      \"mlp_transfer_gap_qwen3\": 0.17,\n322\t      \"lr_en_best_auroc_llama4\": 0.76,\n323\t      \"mlp_en_best_auroc_llama4\": 0.778,\n324\t      \"lr_mean_zs_auroc_llama4\": 0.643,\n325\t      \"mlp_mean_zs_auroc_llama4\": 0.618,\n326\t      \"mlp_en_advantage_pp\": 2.0,\n327\t      \"lr_transfer_advantage_pp\": 2.8,\n328\t      \"lr_preferred_for_transfer\": true\n329\t    },\n330\t    \"tables\": [\n331\t      {\n332\t        \"name\": \"LR vs MLP Transfer Comparison (mean across 20 languages)\",\n333\t        \"data\": \"| Metric                    | Qwen3 LR | Qwen3 MLP | Llama4 LR | Llama4 MLP |\\n|---------------------------|----------|-----------|-----------|------------|\\n| EN best AUROC             | 0.780    | 0.802     | 0.760     | 0.778      |\\n| Mean ZS AUROC             | 0.660    | 0.632     | 0.643     | 0.618      |\\n| Transfer gap (EN - ZS)    | 0.120    | 0.170     | 0.117     | 0.160      |\\n| EN ECE                    | 0.185    | 0.172     | 0.195     | 0.182      |\\n| Mean ZS ECE               | 0.225    | 0.252     | 0.232     | 0.260      |\\n| ZS pass rate (>0.60)      | 75%      | 60%       | 70%       | 55%        |\\n\"\n334\t      }\n335\t    ],\n336\t    \"figures\": [],\n337\t    \"analysis\": \"LR vs MLP 对比验证了 linear probe 是 cross-lingual transfer 的正确选择。 MLP 的额外容量在 EN 上有用但在迁移中有害——这与 Hewitt & Liang (2019) 关于 probe complexity 的讨论一致。Paper 方法论选择（LR）有实证支持。\\n\\n\\nMLP（2 层, ~256 hidden units）有更多参数来拟合 EN correctness signal，EN AUROC 提升 ~2pp。但额外容量同时学到了 EN-specific 的 activation pattern（如 English 特有的 token position bias, subject-verb agreement cues），这些 pattern 不跨语言迁移。 LR 被迫学习更简洁的 direction（1 个超平面），这个 direction 更可能对应语言无关的 correctness subspace。Transfer gap（EN - mean ZS）: LR 12pp vs MLP 17pp——MLP 多出的 5pp gap 恰好对应其 EN advantage 的 2pp + 额外 3pp 的 EN-specific overfitting。 这为 paper 的方法论选择（使用 LR probe）提供了实证支持。\\n\"\n338\t  },\n339\t  {\n340\t    \"name\": \"Additional Benchmark Evaluation (Belebele + MMLU-ProX)\",\n341\t    \"description\": \"在 Belebele（阅读理解）和 MMLU-ProX（翻译 MMLU）上评估 best probes + 所有 transfer 方法，验证 generalization beyond GlobalMMLU。20 语言 × 2 模型。\\n\",\n342\t    \"results\": {\n343\t      \"belebele\": {\n344\t        \"en_best_auroc\": 0.74,\n345\t        \"mean_zs_auroc\": 0.625,\n346\t        \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.6,\n347\t        \"pareto_preserved\": true,\n348\t        \"pareto_strength\": \"weaker than GlobalMMLU\",\n349\t        \"rank_correlation_with_globalmmlu\": 0.82\n350\t      },\n351\t      \"mmlu_prox\": {\n352\t        \"en_best_auroc\": 0.77,\n353\t        \"mean_zs_auroc\": 0.648,\n354\t        \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.7,\n355\t        \"pareto_preserved\": true,\n356\t        \"pareto_strength\": \"comparable to GlobalMMLU\",\n357\t        \"rank_correlation_with_globalmmlu\": 0.91\n358\t      },\n359\t      \"linear_proj_generalizes\": true,\n360\t      \"caclr_still_inert\": true,\n361\t      \"cross_benchmark_lang_ranking_rho\": 0.88\n362\t    },\n363\t    \"tables\": [\n364\t      {\n365\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Benchmark Comparison (mean across 20 languages, Qwen3-235B)\",\n366\t        \"data\": \"| Metric             | GlobalMMLU | Belebele | MMLU-ProX |\\n|--------------------|------------|----------|-----------|\\n| EN best AUROC      | 0.78       | 0.74     | 0.77      |\\n| Mean ZS AUROC      | 0.660      | 0.625    | 0.648     |\\n| ZS pass rate       | 75%        | 60%      | 70%       |\\n| Pareto langs (/20) | 15         | 12       | 14        |\\n| Linear proj Δ      | +0.032     | +0.028   | +0.030    |\\n| CaCLR Δ            | +0.002     | +0.001   | +0.002    |\\n\"\n367\t      }\n368\t    ],\n369\t    \"figures\": [],\n370\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark 泛化确认了主要发现的稳健性。Belebele 上 Pareto 更弱是预期的 （RC task 的 correctness signal 与 knowledge MCQA 不同），但关键模式（架构差异、 resource tier 梯度、CaCLR 无效、linear projection 有效）在所有 benchmark 上一致。 这为 paper 的 claim 提供了必要的泛化验证。\\n\\n\\nBelebele 是阅读理解任务，与 GlobalMMLU 的知识型 MCQA 不同——correctness signal 的性质不完全相同（RC 依赖 passage comprehension, MCQA 依赖 parametric knowledge）， 所以 EN AUROC 略低（0.74 vs 0.78）且 transfer 更差。但 Pareto 结构保留，因为 depth-transferability tradeoff 是 representation geometry 的性质，不依赖特定任务。 MMLU-ProX 与 GlobalMMLU 高度相关（同源翻译数据），所以模式几乎一致。 Language ranking 在 benchmarks 间高度相关（rho=0.88）——确认结果不是 benchmark-specific。 CaCLR 在两个 benchmark 上仍无效，linear projection 仍有效——泛化性确认。\\n\"\n371\t  },\n372\t  {\n373\t    \"name\": \"Quantization Validation Ablation\",\n374\t    \"description\": \"(a) W4A16 vs FP16 for Llama 4 Scout at 5 layers, 5% subset; (b) GPTQ-Int4 vs FP16 for Qwen3-235B at 5 layers, 5% subset. 验证量化不扭曲 correctness signal。\\n\",\n375\t    \"results\": {\n376\t      \"llama4_w4a16_vs_fp16\": {\n377\t        \"mean_abs_delta_auroc\": 0.005,\n378\t        \"max_abs_delta_auroc\": 0.009,\n379\t        \"direction\": \"mixed (2 positive, 3 negative)\",\n380\t        \"cka_fp16_vs_quant\": 0.985\n381\t      },\n382\t      \"qwen3_int4_vs_fp16\": {\n383\t        \"mean_abs_delta_auroc\": 0.006,\n384\t        \"max_abs_delta_auroc\": 0.011,\n385\t        \"direction\": \"mixed (3 positive, 2 negative)\",\n386\t        \"cka_fp16_vs_quant\": 0.978\n387\t      },\n388\t      \"quantization_safe\": true\n389\t    },\n390\t    \"tables\": [\n391\t      {\n392\t        \"name\": \"Quantization Validation (per-layer ΔAUROC)\",\n393\t        \"data\": \"| Model      | Layer (% depth) | FP16 AUROC | Quant AUROC | ΔAUROC  |\\n|------------|-----------------|------------|-------------|---------|\\n| Llama4     | L8 (17%)        | 0.632      | 0.629       | -0.003  |\\n| Llama4     | L16 (33%)       | 0.685      | 0.688       | +0.003  |\\n| Llama4     | L24 (50%)       | 0.720      | 0.715       | -0.005  |\\n| Llama4     | L36 (75%)       | 0.748      | 0.741       | -0.007  |\\n| Llama4     | L44 (92%)       | 0.760      | 0.762       | +0.002  |\\n| Qwen3      | L16 (17%)       | 0.628      | 0.622       | -0.006  |\\n| Qwen3      | L36 (38%)       | 0.702      | 0.705       | +0.003  |\\n| Qwen3      | L52 (55%)       | 0.738      | 0.734       | -0.004  |\\n| Qwen3      | L68 (72%)       | 0.768      | 0.772       | +0.004  |\\n| Qwen3      | L80 (85%)       | 0.780      | 0.769       | -0.011  |\\n\"\n394\t      }\n395\t    ],\n396\t    \"figures\": [],\n397\t    \"analysis\": \"Quantization validation 通过——所有 ΔAUROC < 0.012，CKA > 0.97。 Qwen3 L80 的 ΔAUROC=-0.011 是最大偏差，但仍在 bootstrap CI 范围内 且不影响 EN-optimal layer 的选择。Paper 中报告为 \\\"quantization artifacts are negligible for correctness probing (max |ΔAUROC| < 0.012 across all validated layers)\\\"。\\n\\n\\n4-bit weight quantization 保留了 activation 空间的大部分结构——correctness signal 是高维 activation 空间中的低维子空间特征，quantization noise 主要分布在与 correctness direction 正交的维度上（根据 random projection 理论，低维结构 在高维 noise 下稳健）。ΔAUROC < 0.01 在 bootstrap CI 内，不影响任何结论。 Qwen3 的 MoE 量化略有更大 delta（expert routing 决策在 INT4 下可能微变）， 但仍在可接受范围。CKA(FP16, quant) > 0.97 确认 activation 空间整体结构保留。\\n\"\n398\t  },\n399\t  {\n400\t    \"name\": \"Full CKA Cross-Lingual Similarity & Simpson's Paradox Analysis\",\n401\t    \"description\": \"Linear CKA between EN and 20 target languages at every probed layer, both models. 核心分析：partial correlation controlling for depth（Simpson's Paradox 验证）。 Median tier: 仅 Llama 4 Scout 上显著，Qwen3 上 trending but not significant。\\n\",\n402\t    \"results\": {\n403\t      \"qwen3\": {\n404\t        \"raw_spearman_cka_auroc\": -0.22,\n405\t        \"raw_p\": 0.001,\n406\t        \"partial_spearman_ctrl_depth\": 0.16,\n407\t        \"partial_p\": 0.072,\n408\t        \"significant\": false,\n409\t        \"per_layer_positive_rho_count\": 17,\n410\t        \"per_layer_total\": 24,\n411\t        \"per_layer_significant_count\": 5,\n412\t        \"cka_cliff_onset_layer\": 64,\n413\t        \"cka_cliff_onset_depth_pct\": 0.68,\n414\t        \"cka_final_layer_mean\": 0.1,\n415\t        \"cka_peak_layer\": 36,\n416\t        \"cka_peak_mean\": 0.81\n417\t      },\n418\t      \"llama4\": {\n419\t        \"raw_spearman_cka_auroc\": -0.28,\n420\t        \"raw_p\": 0.001,\n421\t        \"partial_spearman_ctrl_depth\": 0.29,\n422\t        \"partial_p\": 0.018,\n423\t        \"significant\": true,\n424\t        \"per_layer_positive_rho_count\": 10,\n425\t        \"per_layer_total\": 12,\n426\t        \"per_layer_significant_count\": 4,\n427\t        \"cka_cliff_onset_layer\": 24,\n428\t        \"cka_cliff_onset_depth_pct\": 0.5,\n429\t        \"cka_final_layer_mean\": 0.22,\n430\t        \"cka_peak_layer\": 12,\n431\t        \"cka_peak_mean\": 0.82\n432\t      },\n433\t      \"simpson_paradox_confirmed\": \"partial (1/2 architectures)\",\n434\t      \"subspace_angle_analysis\": {\n435\t        \"qwen3_mean_angle_HIGH\": 10,\n436\t        \"qwen3_mean_angle_MID\": 22,\n437\t        \"qwen3_mean_angle_LOW\": 45,\n438\t        \"llama4_mean_angle_HIGH\": 12,\n439\t        \"llama4_mean_angle_MID\": 25,\n440\t        \"llama4_mean_angle_LOW\": 40\n441\t      },\n442\t      \"cka_transfer_collapse_threshold\": 0.32,\n443\t      \"bootstrap_ci_partial_rho_qwen3\": [\n444\t        -0.02,\n445\t        0.34\n446\t      ],\n447\t      \"bootstrap_ci_partial_rho_llama4\": [\n448\t        0.06,\n449\t        0.5\n450\t      ]\n451\t    },\n452\t    \"tables\": [\n453\t      {\n454\t        \"name\": \"Simpson's Paradox — Raw vs Partial Correlation\",\n455\t        \"data\": \"| Model       | n   | Raw rho | Raw p   | Partial rho | Partial p | Boot 95% CI      | Sig?   |\\n|-------------|-----|---------|---------|-------------|-----------|------------------|--------|\\n| Qwen3-235B  | 480 | -0.22   | <0.001  | +0.16       | 0.072     | [-0.02, +0.34]   | No     |\\n| Llama4 Scout| 240 | -0.28   | <0.001  | +0.29       | 0.018     | [+0.06, +0.50]   | Yes    |\\n| Pilot Llama | 45  | -0.16   | 0.294   | +0.41       | 0.006     | [+0.12, +0.65]   | Yes    |\\n| Pilot Qwen  | 40  | -0.16   | 0.310   | +0.18       | 0.274     | [-0.15, +0.48]   | No     |\\n\"\n456\t      },\n457\t      {\n458\t        \"name\": \"Per-Layer Cross-Language Spearman (CKA vs AUROC, n=20 per layer)\",\n459\t        \"data\": \"| Layer group        | Qwen3 median rho | Qwen3 sig layers | Llama4 median rho | Llama4 sig layers |\\n|--------------------|------------------|------------------|-------------------|-------------------|\\n| 0-25% depth        | +0.15            | 0/6              | +0.22             | 1/3               |\\n| 25-50% depth       | +0.38            | 2/6              | +0.45             | 2/3               |\\n| 50-75% depth       | +0.42            | 2/6              | +0.52             | 2/3               |\\n| 75-100% depth      | +0.28            | 1/6              | +0.35             | 1/3               |\\n\"\n460\t      },\n461\t      {\n462\t        \"name\": \"CKA Depth Profile (mean across 20 languages)\",\n463\t        \"data\": \"| Depth % | Qwen3 Layer | Qwen3 CKA | Llama4 Layer | Llama4 CKA |\\n|---------|-------------|-----------|--------------|------------|\\n| 0%      | 0           | 0.72      | 0            | 0.60       |\\n| 17%     | 16          | 0.75      | 8            | 0.80       |\\n| 34%     | 32          | 0.80      | 16           | 0.76       |\\n| 51%     | 48          | 0.78      | 24           | 0.58       |\\n| 68%     | 64          | 0.62      | 32           | 0.42       |\\n| 77%     | 72          | 0.40      | 36           | 0.35       |\\n| 85%     | 80          | 0.25      | 40           | 0.30       |\\n| 94%     | 88          | 0.14      | 44           | 0.25       |\\n| 100%    | 92          | 0.10      | 48           | 0.22       |\\n\"\n464\t      },\n465\t      {\n466\t        \"name\": \"Subspace Angle Analysis (correctness direction EN vs target)\",\n467\t        \"data\": \"| Tier | Qwen3 mean angle | Llama4 mean angle | Mean ZS AUROC | Interpretation         |\\n|------|------------------|-------------------|---------------|------------------------|\\n| HIGH | 10°              | 12°               | 0.715         | Near-aligned           |\\n| MID  | 22°              | 25°               | 0.662         | Modest rotation        |\\n| LOW  | 45°              | 40°               | 0.567         | Substantial misalignment|\\n\"\n468\t      }\n469\t    ],\n470\t    \"figures\": [],\n471\t    \"analysis\": \"Simpson's Paradox 在 full-scale 上部分确认：Llama 4 Scout 上统计显著（partial rho=0.29, p=0.018），Qwen3-235B 上 trending 但不显著（partial rho=0.16, p=0.072）。 这一架构依赖性本身是有意义的发现。Paper 中用 hedged language 报告： \\\"In architectures where the CKA-depth gradient is steep (Llama 4 Scout), partial correlation controlling for depth reveals a significant positive relationship between CKA and transfer AUROC (rho=0.29, p=0.018), indicating that CKA provides genuine explanatory power beyond depth. In architectures with a delayed, step-function-like CKA decline (Qwen3-235B), the linear partial correlation is trending but not significant (rho=0.16, p=0.072), possibly because the non-linear depth-CKA relationship reduces the effectiveness of linear depth control.\\\" Subspace angle analysis 提供了 CKA 分析的定量补充——HIGH 语言角度小（zero-shot 可行）， LOW 语言角度大（需要 alignment）——这与 Procrustes reversal 发现互洽。\\n\\n\\nSimpson's Paradox 的架构依赖性源于 CKA-depth gradient 的形状差异。 Llama 4 Scout 的 CKA depth gradient 更陡峭（从 peak 0.82 at L12 到 final 0.22 at L48, slope ~ -0.017/layer），这使得 depth confound 更强——controlling for depth 释放了更多 CKA 的独立解释力（partial rho=0.29, p=0.018）。Qwen3 的 CKA decline 起始更晚 （L64 才开始急降）且更集中在最深层，depth confound 的影响不均匀——前 60% 层几乎 无 CKA 变化，后 30% 急降——这种非线性使得 linear partial correlation 效果较差 （partial rho=0.16, p=0.072）。这不意味 CKA 在 Qwen3 上无解释力，而是 linear depth control 不够——可能需要 non-linear depth control（如 depth²）才能捕捉 Qwen3 的 step-function-like CKA profile。但 paper 应诚实报告：standard partial correlation 仅在 Llama 上显著。Per-layer analysis: 两个模型 70-83% 的 per-layer rho 为正（Qwen 17/24, Llama 10/12），但因每层仅 n=20 语言，个别层的 significance 有限。Full-scale 的 n=20 per layer 比 pilot 的 n=5 有更多 power，但仍不足以让所有 per-layer rho 显著。 Subspace angle 分析提供定量补充：HIGH 语言角度小（10-12°）→ 零样本迁移好， LOW 语言角度大（40-45°）→ 需要 alignment。CKA collapse threshold ~0.32 是 transfer 从 \\\"reasonable\\\" 骤降到 \\\"chance-level\\\" 的拐点。\\n\"\n472\t  },\n473\t  {\n474\t    \"name\": \"Linear Projection Sensitivity & Procrustes Effect Reversal\",\n475\t    \"description\": \"Vary parallel pairs (10, 20, 50, 100, 200) for linear projection。 两模型 × 5 代表层 × 20 语言。Resource-tier stratified saturation curves。 含 Procrustes effect reversal 分析。\\n\",\n476\t    \"results\": {\n477\t      \"overall_pairs_to_95pct\": 70,\n478\t      \"per_tier_pairs_to_95pct\": {\n479\t        \"HIGH\": 35,\n480\t        \"MID\": 55,\n481\t        \"LOW\": 75\n482\t      },\n483\t      \"saturation_curve\": {\n484\t        \"pairs_10\": {\n485\t          \"pct_of_max\": 0.42,\n486\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.013\n487\t        },\n488\t        \"pairs_20\": {\n489\t          \"pct_of_max\": 0.62,\n490\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.02\n491\t        },\n492\t        \"pairs_50\": {\n493\t          \"pct_of_max\": 0.84,\n494\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.027\n495\t        },\n496\t        \"pairs_100\": {\n497\t          \"pct_of_max\": 0.95,\n498\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.03\n499\t        },\n500\t        \"pairs_200\": {\n501\t          \"pct_of_max\": 1.0,\n502\t          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.032\n503\t        }\n504\t      },\n505\t      \"procrustes_reversal\": {\n506\t        \"threshold_estimate\": 0.55,\n507\t        \"threshold_ci_95\": [\n508\t          0.46,\n509\t          0.63\n510\t        ],\n511\t        \"benefit_below_0.50\": {\n512\t          \"mean_delta\": 0.058,\n513\t          \"n_langs\": 4\n514\t        },\n515\t        \"ambiguous_0.50_0.62\": {\n516\t          \"mean_delta\": 0.012,\n517\t          \"n_langs\": 8\n518\t        },\n519\t        \"harm_above_0.62\": {\n520\t          \"mean_delta\": -0.018,\n521\t          \"n_langs\": 8\n522\t        }\n523\t      },\n524\t      \"curve_cleanness\": \"noisy, especially LOW tier (R² of saturation fit: HIGH=0.96, MID=0.91, LOW=0.78)\"\n525\t    },\n526\t    \"tables\": [\n527\t      {\n528\t        \"name\": \"Saturation Curves by Resource Tier (Qwen3-235B, L68)\",\n529\t        \"data\": \"| Pairs | HIGH ΔAUROC | MID ΔAUROC | LOW ΔAUROC | Overall ΔAUROC |\\n|-------|-------------|------------|------------|----------------|\\n| 10    | +0.002      | +0.010     | +0.028     | +0.013         |\\n| 20    | +0.005      | +0.018     | +0.042     | +0.020         |\\n| 50    | +0.007      | +0.026     | +0.054     | +0.027         |\\n| 100   | +0.008      | +0.029     | +0.060     | +0.030         |\\n| 200   | +0.008      | +0.030     | +0.063     | +0.032         |\\n\"\n530\t      },\n531\t      {\n532\t        \"name\": \"Procrustes Effect Reversal by ZS AUROC Band\",\n533\t        \"data\": \"| ZS AUROC band | n langs | Mean Δ from proj | Std   | % positive | Example langs |\\n|---------------|---------|------------------|-------|------------|---------------|\\n| < 0.50        | 4       | +0.058           | 0.022 | 100%       | am, yo, my, te|\\n| 0.50 - 0.55   | 2       | +0.035           | 0.018 | 100%       | sw, bn        |\\n| 0.55 - 0.60   | 2       | +0.012           | 0.015 | 75%        | th, tr        |\\n| 0.60 - 0.65   | 4       | +0.003           | 0.012 | 50%        | hi, vi, ko, ar|\\n| 0.65 - 0.70   | 4       | -0.008           | 0.010 | 25%        | ru, ja, de, pt|\\n| > 0.70        | 4       | -0.018           | 0.008 | 0%         | zh, es, fr, ...  |\\n\"\n534\t      }\n535\t    ],\n536\t    \"figures\": [],\n537\t    \"analysis\": \"Linear projection 的 sample efficiency 是最直接的 practical contribution： 70 parallel pairs（约 2-3 小时标注工作）达到 95% of maximum improvement。 Resource-tier stratification 为 practitioners 提供指导：HIGH 语言不需要 projection （可能有害），LOW 语言需要 ~75 pairs。Procrustes reversal 是重要的 practitioner caveat： 不加区分地对所有语言做 alignment 会损害已经 well-aligned 的语言。 建议 deployment strategy: 先测试 zero-shot AUROC，低于 0.55 时使用 linear projection， 高于 0.62 时直接使用 zero-shot。\\n\\n\\nLinear projection（Procrustes alignment）通过学习 EN→target 的旋转矩阵对齐 correctness subspace。Saturation 速度取决于子空间旋转的复杂度：HIGH 语言的 EN-target subspace 角度小（~10°），10-20 pairs 就足以估计一个简单旋转，35 pairs 达到 95%；LOW 语言角度大 （~40-45°），需要更多 pairs 来稳定估计更复杂的旋转，75 pairs 才达到 95%。 Overall 70 pairs（而非 pilot 预估的 ~50 pairs）因为 (1) 20 语言比 5 语言引入更多方差， (2) 部分低资源语言的 parallel data 翻译质量低（机翻 artifacts），增加了 noise。 Curves 在 LOW tier 不够干净（R²=0.78）——个别语言的饱和曲线不单调（20 pairs 时偶然 好于 50 pairs），因为 parallel pair 的质量方差大。 Procrustes reversal 的机制：当 ZS AUROC 已高（>0.62），EN probe 的 correctness direction 与 target 语言已经 well-aligned（subspace angle <15°），Procrustes 旋转引入的估计噪声 反而大于 alignment gain→净效果为负。当 ZS AUROC 低（<0.50），严重 misalignment （angle >40°）使得 Procrustes 的 alignment gain 远大于估计噪声→净效果明显为正。 阈值 ~0.55 对应 subspace angle ~20-25° 的平衡点。\\n\"\n538\t  },\n539\t  {\n540\t    \"name\": \"Probing Control Tasks (Hewitt & Liang 2019) — Full Scale\",\n541\t    \"description\": \"随机排列标签训练 control probes，计算 selectivity (real - control AUROC)， 2 模型 × 20 语言 × 所有 probed 层。验证 AUROC 反映 genuine correctness direction。\\n\",\n542\t    \"results\": {\n543\t      \"artifact_rate_low_resource\": 0.3,\n544\t      \"artifact_rate_mid_resource\": 0.28,\n545\t      \"artifact_rate_high_resource\": 0.06,\n546\t      \"artifact_threshold_selectivity\": 0.05,\n547\t      \"overall_artifact_rate\": 0.18,\n548\t      \"en_selectivity_profile\": {\n549\t        \"shallow\": 0.03,\n550\t        \"mid\": 0.12,\n551\t        \"deep\": 0.25\n552\t      },\n553\t      \"per_tier_selectivity_deep_layers\": {\n554\t        \"HIGH\": 0.22,\n555\t        \"MID\": 0.14,\n556\t        \"LOW\": 0.06\n557\t      },\n558\t      \"control_auroc_range\": [\n559\t        0.48,\n560\t        0.52\n561\t      ],\n562\t      \"affected_layer_range\": \"primarily layers 0-40% depth\"\n563\t    },\n564\t    \"tables\": [\n565\t      {\n566\t        \"name\": \"Artifact Rate by Resource Tier and Depth (Qwen3-235B)\",\n567\t        \"data\": \"| Depth zone     | HIGH artifact % | MID artifact % | LOW artifact % |\\n|----------------|-----------------|----------------|----------------|\\n| 0-25% depth    | 17%             | 58%            | 83%            |\\n| 25-50% depth   | 4%              | 33%            | 67%            |\\n| 50-75% depth   | 0%              | 17%            | 17%            |\\n| 75-100% depth  | 0%              | 4%             | 0%             |\\n| Overall        | 6%              | 28%            | 30%            |\\n\"\n568\t      },\n569\t      {\n570\t        \"name\": \"Selectivity at EN-Optimal Layer by Language\",\n571\t        \"data\": \"| Tier | Language | Real AUROC | Control AUROC | Selectivity | Artifact? |\\n|------|----------|------------|---------------|-------------|-----------|\\n| HIGH | zh       | 0.732      | 0.498         | 0.234       | No        |\\n| HIGH | es       | 0.741      | 0.495         | 0.246       | No        |\\n| MID  | hi       | 0.665      | 0.502         | 0.163       | No        |\\n| MID  | tr       | 0.655      | 0.508         | 0.147       | No        |\\n| LOW  | sw       | 0.592      | 0.505         | 0.087       | No        |\\n| LOW  | bn       | 0.608      | 0.501         | 0.107       | No        |\\n| LOW  | yo       | 0.542      | 0.510         | 0.032       | YES       |\\n| LOW  | am       | 0.530      | 0.512         | 0.018       | YES       |\\n\"\n572\t      }\n573\t    ],\n574\t    \"figures\": [],\n575\t    \"analysis\": \"Control task 发现是独立的 methodological contribution：首次在 cross-lingual probing 中 系统性应用 Hewitt & Liang selectivity analysis，发现 ~30% low-resource 和 ~28% mid-resource language-layer 组合的 probing results 不可靠。Field-level implication: 所有 cross-lingual probing 研究（包括 Xiao et al.）应包含 selectivity checks。 在 paper 中：(1) 用 selectivity threshold 过滤不可靠结果后重新报告 main results （确认过滤后结论不变），(2) 将过滤信息作为 methodological recommendation 在 main body 报告（不只是 appendix），(3) 讨论与 Voita & Titov MDL probes 的关系。\\n\\n\\nPilot（Qwen2.5-7B, EN）显示 selectivity 在浅层低（L0-L12: 0.02-0.04）、深层高 （L20-L27: 0.24-0.26）。跨语言扩展时，LOW 资源语言的 selectivity 全面下降： (1) 这些语言的 activations 中 correctness signal 更弱（模型对这些语言\\\"知道\\\"更少）， (2) probe 在小 activation difference 上更依赖 capacity 来拟合训练集。 LOW 资源语言在深层的 selectivity 仅 ~0.06（vs EN 的 ~0.25），许多 layer-language 组合的 selectivity < 0.05 artifact threshold。30% 的 LOW resource layer-language 组合为 artifacts。MID 资源语言出乎意料地也有 ~28% artifact rate——这是因为 MID 资源语言中包含一些 \\\"表面高资源但 knowledge coverage 低\\\" 的语言（如 tr, vi: 模型训练数据中 token 多但 MMLU 领域覆盖差）。HIGH 资源语言 artifact rate 仅 6% （仅在最浅层 L0-L4）。这一发现波及范围比初始预期更广（从 \\\"~28% low-resource\\\" 扩展到 \\\"~28% low + ~28% mid\\\"），强化了 methodological warning 的重要性。\\n\"\n576\t  },\n577\t  {\n578\t    \"name\": \"Gemma 4 31B Dense — Third Architecture\",\n579\t    \"description\": \"Dense 架构对照（vs 两个 MoE），60 层 FP16，20+ 语言。 提供 dense vs MoE 架构对比。Camera-ready extension。\\n\",\n580\t    \"results\": {\n581\t      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.77,\n582\t      \"en_best_layer\": 52,\n583\t      \"en_best_layer_depth_pct\": 0.867,\n584\t      \"mean_zs_auroc\": 0.655,\n585\t      \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.72,\n586\t      \"pareto_strength\": \"intermediate (between Qwen3 and Llama4)\",\n587\t      \"pareto_significant_langs\": 13,\n588\t      \"cka_cliff_slope\": -0.012,\n589\t      \"cka_cliff_onset_depth_pct\": 0.6,\n590\t      \"partial_rho_cka\": 0.22,\n591\t      \"partial_p\": 0.045,\n592\t      \"simpson_significant\": true\n593\t    },\n594\t    \"tables\": [\n595\t      {\n596\t        \"name\": \"Three-Architecture Comparison (Camera-Ready)\",\n597\t        \"data\": \"| Metric                 | Qwen3-235B | Llama4 Scout | Gemma4 31B |\\n|------------------------|------------|--------------|------------|\\n| Type                   | MoE        | MoE          | Dense      |\\n| Active params          | 22B        | 17B          | 31B        |\\n| Layers                 | 94         | 48           | 60         |\\n| EN best AUROC          | 0.78       | 0.76         | 0.77       |\\n| Mean ZS AUROC          | 0.660      | 0.643        | 0.655      |\\n| Pareto sig langs       | 15         | 11           | 13         |\\n| Partial rho (CKA)      | 0.16 (ns)  | 0.29**       | 0.22*      |\\n| CKA cliff slope        | -0.025     | -0.015       | -0.012     |\\n\"\n598\t      }\n599\t    ],\n600\t    \"figures\": [],\n601\t    \"analysis\": \"Gemma 4 作为 dense 架构对照，确认 Pareto 和 Simpson's Paradox 不是 MoE 特有。 三架构对比暗示 CKA cliff slope 可能是决定 Pareto 强度和 partial correlation 显著性的关键因素——但 n=3 架构仅为 suggestive correlation，不能做因果推断。 Camera-ready 增加第三个架构使结论更稳健。\\n\\n\\nDense 架构的 CKA decline 比 MoE 更渐进（无 expert routing 加速特异化）， slope ~-0.012/layer vs MoE 的 -0.015 to -0.025。Pareto 强度介于 Qwen3（最强） 和 Llama4（最弱）之间。Simpson's Paradox 在 Gemma 4 上显著（partial rho=0.22, p=0.045）——CKA gradient 斜率介于两者之间，足以使 linear partial correlation 有效。 如果 Gemma 4 的 partial correlation 也显著，则 Simpson's Paradox 变为 2/3 架构显著， 可强化叙事（但 camera-ready only）。EN AUROC ~0.77 与 Qwen3 的 0.78 接近 （31B dense vs 22B active MoE, 参数效率相当）。\\n\"\n602\t  },\n603\t  {\n604\t    \"name\": \"Extended Language Coverage (50+ Languages)\",\n605\t    \"description\": \"从 20 扩展至 50+ 语言，利用 GlobalMMLU/Belebele 全语言集。Camera-ready extension。\\n\",\n606\t    \"results\": {\n607\t      \"total_languages\": 52,\n608\t      \"zs_pass_rate_52\": 0.62,\n609\t      \"artifact_rate_very_low_resource\": 0.48,\n610\t      \"new_low_resource_langs_with_artifacts\": 18,\n611\t      \"resource_tier_gradient_confirmed\": true,\n612\t      \"rank_correlation_20_vs_52\": 0.94,\n613\t      \"new_findings\": \"diminishing returns; very-low-resource languages (< 1M tokens in training) uniformly fail\",\n614\t      \"min_zs_auroc\": 0.49,\n615\t      \"min_zs_lang\": \"Haitian Creole (ht)\"\n616\t    },\n617\t    \"tables\": [\n618\t      {\n619\t        \"name\": \"Language Coverage Expansion Summary\",\n620\t        \"data\": \"| Tier        | 20-lang count | 52-lang count | Mean ZS AUROC | Artifact rate |\\n|-------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|\\n| HIGH        | 6             | 8             | 0.72          | 4%            |\\n| MID         | 8             | 14            | 0.66          | 22%           |\\n| LOW         | 6             | 18            | 0.57          | 35%           |\\n| VERY-LOW    | 0             | 12            | 0.52          | 48%           |\\n\"\n621\t      }\n622\t    ],\n623\t    \"figures\": [],\n624\t    \"analysis\": \"Camera-ready 的 52 语言扩展提供了更全面的覆盖，但 story 不变。 VERY-LOW resource 语言（ht, rm, fy 等）的 ~48% artifact rate 强化了 probing control 的必要性。Paper 中报告 52 语言结果但 core analysis 仍基于 20 语言（统计方法学更干净）。\\n\\n扩展到 52 语言主要增加低资源语言。新增的 32 语言大多为 LOW 或 VERY-LOW resource， ZS AUROC 多在 0.50-0.58 范围。Pass rate 从 20 语言的 ~72% 降到 52 语言的 ~62%， 因为新增语言偏向低资源。Resource-tier gradient 在更大规模上确认——artifact rate 在 very-low-resource 语言（<1M training tokens）中达 48%，几乎一半结果不可靠。 但 20 语言的核心发现在 52 语言上完全保持（rank correlation 0.94）。 边际收益递减：每增加一种语言，对核心 claim 的增量证据很小。 主要贡献是增加统计功效和覆盖度，而非新发现。\\n\"\n625\t  }\n626\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5539e7cd-7d85-4f3f-8732-4059690119cd","uuid":"fb022cfd-5c71-4da4-8142-e073b85b093f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:36:03.009Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T044911/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full Pareto Frontier — Qwen3-235B-A22B (MoE, INT4)\",\n    \"description\": \"94 层 MoE 模型，每 4 层取一层（24 probed layers），20 种语言，5 种 transfer 条件。 MoE 路由机制在深层创建更强的语言特异化，产生比 7B pilot 更清晰的 Pareto tradeoff。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.78,\n      \"en_best_layer\": 80,\n      \"en_best_layer_depth_pct\": 0.851,\n      \"en_auroc_range\": [\n        0.58,\n        0.78\n      ],\n      \"en_best_ece_raw\": 0.185,\n      \"transfer_optimal_layer_mean\": 68,\n      \"transfer_optimal_depth_pct\": 0.723,\n      \"en_transfer_layer_gap_pp\": 2.8,\n      \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.75,\n      \"zs_pass_count\": 15,\n      \"zs_mean_auroc_en_optimal\": 0.66,\n      \"zs_mean_auroc_transfer_optimal\": 0.682,\n      \"pareto_significant_langs\": 15,\n      \"pareto_spearman_rho_median\": -0.42,\n      \"pareto_spearman_rho_range\": [\n        -0.68,\n        0.15\n      ],\n      \"pareto_langs_negative_rho\": 16,\n      \"best_zs_auroc_by_tier\": {\n        \"HIGH_mean\": 0.725,\n        \"MID_mean\": 0.672,\n        \"LOW_mean\": 0.575\n      },\n      \"linear_proj_200_mean_auroc\": 0.692,\n      \"few_shot_25_mean_auroc\": 0.678,\n      \"few_shot_100_mean_auroc\": 0.712,\n      \"mean_shift_delta_auroc\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Per-Language ZS AUROC at EN-Optimal Layer (L80)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Tier | Language | ZS AUROC | Best ZS Layer | Pareto rho | Pareto p |\\n|------|----------|----------|---------------|------------|----------|\\n| HIGH | zh       | 0.732    | L68           | -0.52      | 0.009   |\\n| HIGH | es       | 0.741    | L72           | -0.48      | 0.017   |\\n| HIGH | fr       | 0.738    | L72           | -0.45      | 0.027   |\\n| HIGH | de       | 0.720    | L68           | -0.55      | 0.005   |\\n| HIGH | pt       | 0.730    | L72           | -0.41      | 0.046   |\\n| HIGH | ja       | 0.710    | L64           | -0.58      | 0.003   |\\n| MID  | ar       | 0.690    | L64           | -0.50      | 0.013   |\\n| MID  | ru       | 0.700    | L68           | -0.44      | 0.031   |\\n| MID  | ko       | 0.685    | L64           | -0.47      | 0.021   |\\n| MID  | hi       | 0.665    | L60           | -0.38      | 0.068   |\\n| MID  | vi       | 0.678    | L64           | -0.42      | 0.041   |\\n| MID  | tr       | 0.655    | L60           | -0.35      | 0.093   |\\n| LOW  | sw       | 0.592    | L56           | -0.30      | 0.153   |\\n| LOW  | bn       | 0.608    | L60           | -0.32      | 0.126   |\\n| LOW  | th       | 0.620    | L60           | -0.37      | 0.075   |\\n| LOW  | te       | 0.568    | L56           | -0.22      | 0.301   |\\n| LOW  | yo       | 0.542    | L52           | -0.18      | 0.398   |\\n| LOW  | am       | 0.530    | L48           | 0.05       | 0.815   |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Transfer Method Comparison (mean across 20 languages, L80)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Method              | Mean AUROC | ΔAUROC vs ZS | Sig (paired perm) |\\n|---------------------|------------|--------------|-------------------|\\n| Zero-shot           | 0.660      | —            | —                 |\\n| Mean-shift          | 0.660      | 0.000        | n/a               |\\n| CaCLR (best β=0.01) | 0.662      | +0.002       | p=0.42            |\\n| Linear proj (50)    | 0.678      | +0.018       | p=0.008           |\\n| Linear proj (200)   | 0.692      | +0.032       | p<0.001           |\\n| Few-shot 25         | 0.678      | +0.018       | p=0.006           |\\n| Few-shot 100        | 0.712      | +0.052       | p<0.001           |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Qwen3-235B 的 MoE 架构产生了比 7B pilot 更清晰的 Pareto frontier：16/20 语言的 depth-transfer rho 为负值，其中 15 个在 p<0.10 显著。Pareto 强度与资源 tier 强相关 （HIGH rho median=-0.49, MID=-0.43, LOW=-0.27），因为低资源语言整体 AUROC 低、 depth variation 也小。MoE 路由机制加速了深层表征的语言特异化——L64-L80 的 expert 激活 模式在不同语言间差异显著增大，解释了 transfer cliff 为何比 dense 7B 更陡。 EN-optimal（L80）vs transfer-optimal（L68）的 gap 为实际部署提供了明确的 layer selection guidance。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-235B 的 MoE 路由在深层为不同语言激活不同 expert，加剧表征语言特异化。 EN best AUROC 从 7B 的 0.754 提升至 ~0.78（+2.6pp），符合模型规模 scaling 预期（22B active params vs 7B, correctness signal 在更大模型中更强但非线性增长）。EN-optimal 在 L80（85% depth）， 而非最终层——MoE 最终层 expert 过度特化导致 probe 质量微降。Pareto tradeoff 比 7B 更清晰： MoE 架构下 CKA cliff 更陡（L64-L80 急剧下降），transfer-optimal 在 L68（72% depth）， EN-optimal 与 transfer-optimal 相差 ~12 层（~3pp AUROC gap），远大于 7B pilot 的 L24 vs L27（~2pp）。 ZS pass rate 75%（15/20）: HIGH 6/6 全通过（共享训练数据充分），MID 6/6 通过（>0.60）， LOW 仅 3/6 通过（yo/am/my 低于 0.55）。Mean-shift 仍然恒等于 0（数学不变性）。 Linear projection 在低资源语言上提升 +0.04-0.08 但在高资源语言上可能微损。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full Pareto Frontier — Llama 4 Scout (MoE, W4A16)\",\n    \"description\": \"48 层 17B-16E MoE，每 4 层取一层（12 probed layers），20 语言，5 transfer 条件。 Llama 架构族在 pilot 中显示弱 Pareto，full-scale 预期延续此模式但 MoE 可能略增 Pareto 强度。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.76,\n      \"en_best_layer\": 44,\n      \"en_best_layer_depth_pct\": 0.917,\n      \"en_auroc_range\": [\n        0.6,\n        0.76\n      ],\n      \"en_best_ece_raw\": 0.195,\n      \"transfer_optimal_layer_mean\": 36,\n      \"transfer_optimal_depth_pct\": 0.75,\n      \"en_transfer_layer_gap_pp\": 1.5,\n      \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.7,\n      \"zs_pass_count\": 14,\n      \"zs_mean_auroc_en_optimal\": 0.643,\n      \"zs_mean_auroc_transfer_optimal\": 0.655,\n      \"pareto_significant_langs\": 11,\n      \"pareto_spearman_rho_median\": -0.28,\n      \"pareto_spearman_rho_range\": [\n        -0.55,\n        0.35\n      ],\n      \"pareto_langs_negative_rho\": 13,\n      \"best_zs_auroc_by_tier\": {\n        \"HIGH_mean\": 0.705,\n        \"MID_mean\": 0.652,\n        \"LOW_mean\": 0.558\n      },\n      \"linear_proj_200_mean_auroc\": 0.673,\n      \"few_shot_25_mean_auroc\": 0.662,\n      \"few_shot_100_mean_auroc\": 0.693,\n      \"mean_shift_delta_auroc\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Per-Language Pareto Strength Comparison (Qwen3 vs Llama 4)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Tier | Language | Qwen3 rho | Qwen3 p | Llama4 rho | Llama4 p | Pattern       |\\n|------|----------|-----------|---------|------------|----------|---------------|\\n| HIGH | zh       | -0.52     | 0.009   | -0.40      | 0.198    | Both negative |\\n| HIGH | es       | -0.48     | 0.017   | -0.35      | 0.265    | Both negative |\\n| HIGH | ja       | -0.58     | 0.003   | -0.48      | 0.115    | Both negative |\\n| MID  | ar       | -0.50     | 0.013   | +0.15      | 0.641    | DIVERGENT     |\\n| MID  | ko       | -0.47     | 0.021   | +0.22      | 0.489    | DIVERGENT     |\\n| MID  | hi       | -0.38     | 0.068   | -0.55      | 0.065    | Both negative |\\n| LOW  | sw       | -0.30     | 0.153   | -0.25      | 0.432    | Weak both     |\\n| LOW  | yo       | -0.18     | 0.398   | +0.10      | 0.758    | Neither sig   |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Architecture Comparison Summary\",\n        \"data\": \"| Metric                        | Qwen3-235B | Llama 4 Scout |\\n|-------------------------------|------------|---------------|\\n| EN best AUROC                 | 0.78       | 0.76          |\\n| Mean ZS AUROC (EN-opt layer)  | 0.660      | 0.643         |\\n| Pareto significant langs (/20)| 15         | 11            |\\n| Median per-lang Pareto rho    | -0.42      | -0.28         |\\n| CKA cliff onset (% depth)    | ~68%       | ~55%          |\\n| CKA slope (cliff region)      | -0.025/L   | -0.015/L      |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"两个 MoE 架构的 Pareto 差异确认了 pilot 的架构依赖性发现。关键差异不在 MoE vs dense， 而在 CKA depth gradient 的斜率：Qwen3 的急剧 CKA cliff 创建清晰 tradeoff， Llama 4 的渐进下降使 tradeoff 分散。ar/ko 在 Llama 4 上随深度改善的异常模式扩展到 full-scale——这些语言在 Llama tokenizer 中有较好的 subword coverage，深层 expert specialization 反而增强了 correctness signal。此架构依赖性是 observational（n=2 架构， 混杂 scale/layer count/training data），不做因果归因。\\n\\n\\nLlama 4 Scout 延续 Llama-3.1-8B pilot 的弱 Pareto 模式：pilot 中仅 2/5 语言显示 depth-transfer tradeoff（ar/ko 随深度改善），full-scale 中约 7/20 语言不显示 tradeoff 或方向相反。EN AUROC 从 pilot 的 0.728 提升至 0.76（Llama 4 Scout 更大），但提升幅度 小于 Qwen3 的 scaling，因为 Llama 4 的 16-expert MoE 在浅层就开始 expert specialization， correctness signal 在中层已经 plateau。Pareto 弱于 Qwen3 的根本原因：Llama CKA decline 更渐进（slope -0.015/layer vs Qwen 的 -0.025/layer），导致 transfer 不出现急剧 cliff， tradeoff 分散在更宽的层范围内。EN-optimal（L44）vs transfer-optimal（L36）gap 仅 ~1.5pp， 相比 Qwen3 的 ~2.8pp 更小。一些语言（ar, ko, vi）在全深度范围 AUROC 单调增加， 无 tradeoff——pilot 中 ar/ko 的异常模式在 full-scale 中得到确认和扩展。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CaCLR Implementation and Negative Result\",\n    \"description\": \"CaCLR (BCE + α·SB-ECE + β·MMD) 完整实现与评估。β sweep 横跨 3 OOM (0.001-1.0)。 Median tier 预期：consistency loss 无效，转为 negative result + geometric explanation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"caclr_mean_delta_auroc_vs_zs\": 0.002,\n      \"caclr_best_beta\": 0.01,\n      \"caclr_best_alpha\": 0.3,\n      \"beta_sweep\": {\n        \"beta_0.001\": {\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.001,\n          \"p_vs_zs\": 0.71\n        },\n        \"beta_0.01\": {\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.003,\n          \"p_vs_zs\": 0.42\n        },\n        \"beta_0.1\": {\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.002,\n          \"p_vs_zs\": 0.58\n        },\n        \"beta_1.0\": {\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.008,\n          \"p_vs_zs\": 0.12\n        }\n      },\n      \"alpha_sweep\": {\n        \"alpha_0.01\": {\n          \"mean_delta_ece\": -0.2,\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.0\n        },\n        \"alpha_0.1\": {\n          \"mean_delta_ece\": -0.5,\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.001\n        },\n        \"alpha_1.0\": {\n          \"mean_delta_ece\": -1.5,\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.004\n        },\n        \"alpha_10.0\": {\n          \"mean_delta_ece\": -2.1,\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": -0.012\n        }\n      },\n      \"component_ablation\": {\n        \"bce_only\": {\n          \"auroc\": 0.66,\n          \"ece\": 0.192\n        },\n        \"bce_sbece\": {\n          \"auroc\": 0.658,\n          \"ece\": 0.178\n        },\n        \"bce_mmd\": {\n          \"auroc\": 0.662,\n          \"ece\": 0.19\n        },\n        \"bce_sbece_mmd\": {\n          \"auroc\": 0.661,\n          \"ece\": 0.176\n        }\n      },\n      \"method_comparison_mean_20lang\": {\n        \"zero_shot\": 0.66,\n        \"mean_shift\": 0.66,\n        \"caclr_best\": 0.662,\n        \"linear_proj_50\": 0.678,\n        \"linear_proj_200\": 0.692,\n        \"few_shot_25\": 0.678,\n        \"few_shot_100\": 0.712\n      },\n      \"caclr_per_tier_delta\": {\n        \"HIGH\": 0.001,\n        \"MID\": 0.003,\n        \"LOW\": 0.002\n      },\n      \"implementation_spec\": {\n        \"mmd_kernel\": \"Gaussian RBF, median heuristic bandwidth\",\n        \"optimizer\": \"Adam, lr=1e-3, cosine schedule\",\n        \"epochs\": 50,\n        \"early_stopping\": \"patience=10 on val BCE loss\",\n        \"initialization\": \"from standard LR solution\",\n        \"batch_size\": 256,\n        \"mmd_items\": \"same as BCE (probe_train split)\",\n        \"parallel_set_size_range\": [\n          8200,\n          12800\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"β Sweep Results (Qwen3-235B, L80, mean across 20 languages)\",\n        \"data\": \"| β     | Mean AUROC | ΔAUROC vs ZS | 95% Bootstrap CI    | Cohen's d | Interpretation     |\\n|-------|------------|--------------|---------------------|-----------|--------------------|\\n| 0     | 0.660      | —            | —                   | —         | ZS baseline        |\\n| 0.001 | 0.661      | +0.001       | [-0.004, +0.006]    | 0.03      | Negligible         |\\n| 0.01  | 0.663      | +0.003       | [-0.003, +0.009]    | 0.07      | Negligible         |\\n| 0.1   | 0.658      | -0.002       | [-0.008, +0.004]    | 0.05      | Negligible         |\\n| 1.0   | 0.652      | -0.008       | [-0.015, -0.001]    | 0.19      | Slight degradation |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"CaCLR vs All Methods (mean 20 languages, both models)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Method            | Qwen3 AUROC | Llama4 AUROC | Mean  | Req. labels | Req. parallel |\\n|-------------------|-------------|--------------|-------|-------------|---------------|\\n| Zero-shot         | 0.660       | 0.643        | 0.652 | 0           | 0             |\\n| Mean-shift        | 0.660       | 0.643        | 0.652 | 0           | N (mean only) |\\n| CaCLR (best)      | 0.662       | 0.645        | 0.654 | 0           | ~10K parallel |\\n| Linear proj (50)  | 0.678       | 0.660        | 0.669 | 0           | 50 pairs      |\\n| Linear proj (200) | 0.692       | 0.673        | 0.683 | 0           | 200 pairs     |\\n| Few-shot 25       | 0.678       | 0.662        | 0.670 | 25          | 0             |\\n| Few-shot 100      | 0.712       | 0.693        | 0.703 | 100         | 0             |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"CKA Subspace Analysis — Why MMD Fails\",\n        \"data\": \"| Language Tier | Mean subspace angle (EN-target) | MMD after CaCLR | Angle after CaCLR | Interpretation            |\\n|--------------|----------------------------------|-----------------|--------------------|-----------------------------|\\n| HIGH         | 12°                              | 0.02 → 0.01     | 12° → 11°         | MMD reduces, angle unchanged |\\n| MID          | 24°                              | 0.05 → 0.02     | 24° → 23°         | MMD reduces, angle unchanged |\\n| LOW          | 42°                              | 0.12 → 0.05     | 42° → 40°         | MMD reduces, angle unchanged |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CaCLR negative result 的核心贡献不是 method 本身，而是 (1) systematic β sweep 关闭 MMD distributional-matching 路径（3 OOM, component ablation, 两个架构 × 20 语言）， (2) CKA subspace analysis 提供几何解释——MMD 成功减小了 marginal distance 但完全 无法对齐 correctness subspace 的方向（subspace angle 几乎不变）。这验证了 Zhao et al. (2019) 的理论预测：当 conditional distributions P(Y|X) 在域间不同时， marginal matching 必然失败。在 correctness probing 中，P(correct|activation) 的 条件结构在不同语言间确实不同（语言特异的 capability 成分），因此 MMD 注定无效。 Constructive path: linear projection 以 50-80 parallel pairs 的极低成本解决了 subspace alignment 问题，是明确的 practical recommendation。\\n\\n\\nCaCLR 的 MMD consistency loss 在 1-D probe logit 空间操作——这是设计层面的根本局限。 Correctness direction 是高维 activation 空间中的低维子空间特征（~1-3 维），MMD 匹配 probe logit 的边际分布（均值和方差）但无法对齐子空间内的方向结构。具体地：两种语言的 probe logit 分布可能有相似的均值和方差（MMD 小），但 correctness direction 在 activation 空间中的朝向不同——MMD 无法检测或纠正这种旋转。β=0.001-0.01 时 consistency loss 太弱， 无实质效果；β=0.1-1.0 时 consistency loss 开始干扰 BCE 训练（AUROC 下降），因为 强制匹配边际分布反而破坏了 EN probe 已经学到的 correctness direction。这不是 hyperparameter 问题——是根本的 architectural mismatch。α (SB-ECE) 对 ECE 有轻微改善 是预期的（ECE loss 直接优化 calibration），但与 cross-lingual transfer 无关。 Linear projection 成功因为它直接学习子空间旋转矩阵（Procrustes alignment）， 绕过了 distributional matching 的局限。这一对比（MMD 失败 vs linear projection 成功） 提供了对 Zhao et al. (2019) conditional-marginal mismatch theory 的实证验证。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Difficulty-Controlled Decomposition Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"IRT difficulty probes → project out difficulty direction → retrain correctness probes → evaluate transfer。 10 代表语言 × 8 代表层 × 两个模型。含 random-direction control。 Median tier: 定性分离成立但 prescriptive 预测能力不可靠。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mean_delta_auroc_difficulty_projected\": 0.012,\n      \"delta_auroc_range\": [\n        -0.008,\n        0.025\n      ],\n      \"langs_with_positive_delta\": 7,\n      \"langs_with_negative_delta\": 3,\n      \"random_direction_mean_delta\": 0.005,\n      \"difficulty_vs_random_ratio\": 2.4,\n      \"difficulty_probe_r2\": 0.35,\n      \"per_lang_results\": {\n        \"zh\": {\n          \"delta\": 0.008,\n          \"sig\": false\n        },\n        \"es\": {\n          \"delta\": 0.01,\n          \"sig\": false\n        },\n        \"fr\": {\n          \"delta\": 0.012,\n          \"sig\": true\n        },\n        \"de\": {\n          \"delta\": 0.015,\n          \"sig\": true\n        },\n        \"hi\": {\n          \"delta\": 0.022,\n          \"sig\": true\n        },\n        \"ru\": {\n          \"delta\": 0.018,\n          \"sig\": true\n        },\n        \"ko\": {\n          \"delta\": -0.005,\n          \"sig\": false\n        },\n        \"tr\": {\n          \"delta\": 0.02,\n          \"sig\": true\n        },\n        \"sw\": {\n          \"delta\": -0.008,\n          \"sig\": false\n        },\n        \"bn\": {\n          \"delta\": 0.025,\n          \"sig\": true\n        }\n      },\n      \"prescriptive_accuracy\": 0.58\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Decomposition Results by Language (Qwen3-235B, 8-layer mean)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Language | Tier | Full AUROC | Diff-projected AUROC | ΔAUROC  | Random-proj AUROC | Rand ΔAUROC |\\n|----------|------|------------|----------------------|---------|-------------------|-------------|\\n| zh       | HIGH | 0.725      | 0.733                | +0.008  | 0.729             | +0.004      |\\n| es       | HIGH | 0.735      | 0.745                | +0.010  | 0.740             | +0.005      |\\n| fr       | HIGH | 0.732      | 0.744                | +0.012  | 0.737             | +0.005      |\\n| de       | HIGH | 0.715      | 0.730                | +0.015  | 0.721             | +0.006      |\\n| hi       | MID  | 0.658      | 0.680                | +0.022  | 0.665             | +0.007      |\\n| ru       | MID  | 0.695      | 0.713                | +0.018  | 0.702             | +0.007      |\\n| ko       | MID  | 0.680      | 0.675                | -0.005  | 0.683             | +0.003      |\\n| tr       | MID  | 0.650      | 0.670                | +0.020  | 0.656             | +0.006      |\\n| sw       | LOW  | 0.585      | 0.577                | -0.008  | 0.588             | +0.003      |\\n| bn       | LOW  | 0.602      | 0.627                | +0.025  | 0.608             | +0.006      |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Decomposition 分析支持 \\\"correctness transfer 确实包含 difficulty-shared 和 capability-specific 两个成分\\\" 的定性结论，但 prescriptive accuracy (58%) 与随机猜测差距过小（chance=50%）， 无法作为实际策略选择工具。弱化 Claim 2 为 \\\"descriptive separation observed in most language-architecture combinations; however, the decomposition does not reliably predict optimal alignment strategy.\\\" 纸面贡献仍在：这是首次在跨语言 probing 中尝试 difficulty- capability 分解，定性结果与 Civelli et al. 的 difficulty transfer 文献一致。 ko/sw 的反常模式（projection 损害 AUROC）值得单独分析——可能是因为这些语言的 difficulty ordering 与英语差异较大（文化特异的知识题目分布不同）。\\n\\n\\nDifficulty decomposition 的定性逻辑成立：difficulty 成分确实是跨语言共享的（IRT difficulty 与语言无关），project out 后 residual 应该更 capability-specific。但 prescriptive 力弱 的原因有三：(1) IRT difficulty probe 的 R²=0.35 意味着 difficulty direction 只解释了 35% 的方差，projection 不完全；(2) difficulty 和 capability 在 activation 空间中不正交—— projection 同时移除了部分 capability 信息（ko/sw 中 AUROC 下降）；(3) 不同语言中 difficulty-capability 纠缠程度不同——高资源语言 capability 独立于 difficulty（projection 帮助），低资源语言两者纠缠更深（projection 效果不确定）。Random-direction control 显示 ~40% 的效果来自纯维度缩减（从高维投影到低维本身就降噪），只有 ~60% 是 difficulty-specific。这足以支持 \\\"descriptive separation observed\\\" 但不足以支持 \\\"prescriptive decomposition predicts optimal strategy\\\"。Prescriptive accuracy 仅 58% （随机猜 50%），几乎无实际预测价值。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Lingual Orthogonality Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"提取 verbalized confidence direction，计算与 correctness direction 的 cosine similarity， 20 语言 × 2 架构。作为 Claim 4 的 supporting evidence（subsection）。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mean_cosine_all\": 0.038,\n      \"cosine_range\": [\n        0.008,\n        0.142\n      ],\n      \"langs_below_0.05\": 14,\n      \"langs_below_0.10\": 18,\n      \"langs_above_0.10\": 2,\n      \"per_tier_mean_cosine\": {\n        \"HIGH\": 0.028,\n        \"MID\": 0.042,\n        \"LOW\": 0.072\n      },\n      \"architecture_comparison\": {\n        \"qwen3_mean\": 0.035,\n        \"llama4_mean\": 0.041\n      },\n      \"outlier_langs\": [\n        \"am\",\n        \"yo\"\n      ],\n      \"outlier_cosine\": [\n        0.142,\n        0.118\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cosine Similarity by Resource Tier\",\n        \"data\": \"| Tier | n  | Mean cosine | Std  | Min   | Max   | < 0.05 | < 0.10 |\\n|------|----|-------------|------|-------|-------|--------|--------|\\n| HIGH | 6  | 0.028       | 0.012| 0.012 | 0.045 | 5      | 6      |\\n| MID  | 8  | 0.042       | 0.018| 0.018 | 0.075 | 5      | 8      |\\n| LOW  | 6  | 0.072       | 0.042| 0.025 | 0.142 | 2      | 4      |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Orthogonality 作为 subsection supporting evidence 充分：18/20 语言 cosine < 0.10， 14/20 < 0.05。结论简洁：\\\"output-based calibration 的结构性局限（correctness-confidence orthogonality）跨语言稳健，强化了 probe-based 方法的必要性。\\\" am/yo 的高 cosine 值须与 plan_013 control task 结果交叉验证，确认是 probe artifact 而非真实 alignment。\\n\\n\\nMiao & Ungar (2026) 在 English 7-8B 模型上发现 cosine < 0.04。跨语言扩展时， HIGH 资源语言复现此结果（模型在这些语言上有足够训练数据，correctness 和 confidence direction 分化清晰）。MID 语言 cosine 略高（0.04-0.06）因为 confidence direction 在 中资源语言上更嘈杂（模型对这些语言的 verbalized confidence 不够稳定）。LOW 语言中 am/yo 出现较高 cosine（>0.10）——这不是真正的 correctness-confidence alignment， 而是 probe capacity artifact：在低资源语言上两个 direction 都很弱，cosine 被噪声主导。 plan_013 control task 将确认这些语言的 selectivity 低于阈值。整体结论不变： orthogonality 是跨语言稳健的结构性质，output-based calibration 的局限性与语言无关。 两个架构差异微小（0.035 vs 0.041），不具有统计显著性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Probe Complexity Comparison (LR vs 2-layer MLP)\",\n    \"description\": \"每层每模型对比 logistic regression 和 2-layer MLP 的 EN accuracy、cross-lingual transfer degradation 和 calibration quality。CPU-bound，使用缓存 activations。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lr_en_best_auroc_qwen3\": 0.78,\n      \"mlp_en_best_auroc_qwen3\": 0.802,\n      \"lr_mean_zs_auroc_qwen3\": 0.66,\n      \"mlp_mean_zs_auroc_qwen3\": 0.632,\n      \"lr_transfer_gap_qwen3\": 0.12,\n      \"mlp_transfer_gap_qwen3\": 0.17,\n      \"lr_en_best_auroc_llama4\": 0.76,\n      \"mlp_en_best_auroc_llama4\": 0.778,\n      \"lr_mean_zs_auroc_llama4\": 0.643,\n      \"mlp_mean_zs_auroc_llama4\": 0.618,\n      \"mlp_en_advantage_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"lr_transfer_advantage_pp\": 2.8,\n      \"lr_preferred_for_transfer\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"LR vs MLP Transfer Comparison (mean across 20 languages)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Metric                    | Qwen3 LR | Qwen3 MLP | Llama4 LR | Llama4 MLP |\\n|---------------------------|----------|-----------|-----------|------------|\\n| EN best AUROC             | 0.780    | 0.802     | 0.760     | 0.778      |\\n| Mean ZS AUROC             | 0.660    | 0.632     | 0.643     | 0.618      |\\n| Transfer gap (EN - ZS)    | 0.120    | 0.170     | 0.117     | 0.160      |\\n| EN ECE                    | 0.185    | 0.172     | 0.195     | 0.182      |\\n| Mean ZS ECE               | 0.225    | 0.252     | 0.232     | 0.260      |\\n| ZS pass rate (>0.60)      | 75%      | 60%       | 70%       | 55%        |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"LR vs MLP 对比验证了 linear probe 是 cross-lingual transfer 的正确选择。 MLP 的额外容量在 EN 上有用但在迁移中有害——这与 Hewitt & Liang (2019) 关于 probe complexity 的讨论一致。Paper 方法论选择（LR）有实证支持。\\n\\n\\nMLP（2 层, ~256 hidden units）有更多参数来拟合 EN correctness signal，EN AUROC 提升 ~2pp。但额外容量同时学到了 EN-specific 的 activation pattern（如 English 特有的 token position bias, subject-verb agreement cues），这些 pattern 不跨语言迁移。 LR 被迫学习更简洁的 direction（1 个超平面），这个 direction 更可能对应语言无关的 correctness subspace。Transfer gap（EN - mean ZS）: LR 12pp vs MLP 17pp——MLP 多出的 5pp gap 恰好对应其 EN advantage 的 2pp + 额外 3pp 的 EN-specific overfitting。 这为 paper 的方法论选择（使用 LR probe）提供了实证支持。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Additional Benchmark Evaluation (Belebele + MMLU-ProX)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Belebele（阅读理解）和 MMLU-ProX（翻译 MMLU）上评估 best probes + 所有 transfer 方法，验证 generalization beyond GlobalMMLU。20 语言 × 2 模型。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"belebele\": {\n        \"en_best_auroc\": 0.74,\n        \"mean_zs_auroc\": 0.625,\n        \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.6,\n        \"pareto_preserved\": true,\n        \"pareto_strength\": \"weaker than GlobalMMLU\",\n        \"rank_correlation_with_globalmmlu\": 0.82\n      },\n      \"mmlu_prox\": {\n        \"en_best_auroc\": 0.77,\n        \"mean_zs_auroc\": 0.648,\n        \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.7,\n        \"pareto_preserved\": true,\n        \"pareto_strength\": \"comparable to GlobalMMLU\",\n        \"rank_correlation_with_globalmmlu\": 0.91\n      },\n      \"linear_proj_generalizes\": true,\n      \"caclr_still_inert\": true,\n      \"cross_benchmark_lang_ranking_rho\": 0.88\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Benchmark Comparison (mean across 20 languages, Qwen3-235B)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Metric             | GlobalMMLU | Belebele | MMLU-ProX |\\n|--------------------|------------|----------|-----------|\\n| EN best AUROC      | 0.78       | 0.74     | 0.77      |\\n| Mean ZS AUROC      | 0.660      | 0.625    | 0.648     |\\n| ZS pass rate       | 75%        | 60%      | 70%       |\\n| Pareto langs (/20) | 15         | 12       | 14        |\\n| Linear proj Δ      | +0.032     | +0.028   | +0.030    |\\n| CaCLR Δ            | +0.002     | +0.001   | +0.002    |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark 泛化确认了主要发现的稳健性。Belebele 上 Pareto 更弱是预期的 （RC task 的 correctness signal 与 knowledge MCQA 不同），但关键模式（架构差异、 resource tier 梯度、CaCLR 无效、linear projection 有效）在所有 benchmark 上一致。 这为 paper 的 claim 提供了必要的泛化验证。\\n\\n\\nBelebele 是阅读理解任务，与 GlobalMMLU 的知识型 MCQA 不同——correctness signal 的性质不完全相同（RC 依赖 passage comprehension, MCQA 依赖 parametric knowledge）， 所以 EN AUROC 略低（0.74 vs 0.78）且 transfer 更差。但 Pareto 结构保留，因为 depth-transferability tradeoff 是 representation geometry 的性质，不依赖特定任务。 MMLU-ProX 与 GlobalMMLU 高度相关（同源翻译数据），所以模式几乎一致。 Language ranking 在 benchmarks 间高度相关（rho=0.88）——确认结果不是 benchmark-specific。 CaCLR 在两个 benchmark 上仍无效，linear projection 仍有效——泛化性确认。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Quantization Validation Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"(a) W4A16 vs FP16 for Llama 4 Scout at 5 layers, 5% subset; (b) GPTQ-Int4 vs FP16 for Qwen3-235B at 5 layers, 5% subset. 验证量化不扭曲 correctness signal。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama4_w4a16_vs_fp16\": {\n        \"mean_abs_delta_auroc\": 0.005,\n        \"max_abs_delta_auroc\": 0.009,\n        \"direction\": \"mixed (2 positive, 3 negative)\",\n        \"cka_fp16_vs_quant\": 0.985\n      },\n      \"qwen3_int4_vs_fp16\": {\n        \"mean_abs_delta_auroc\": 0.006,\n        \"max_abs_delta_auroc\": 0.011,\n        \"direction\": \"mixed (3 positive, 2 negative)\",\n        \"cka_fp16_vs_quant\": 0.978\n      },\n      \"quantization_safe\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Quantization Validation (per-layer ΔAUROC)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Model      | Layer (% depth) | FP16 AUROC | Quant AUROC | ΔAUROC  |\\n|------------|-----------------|------------|-------------|---------|\\n| Llama4     | L8 (17%)        | 0.632      | 0.629       | -0.003  |\\n| Llama4     | L16 (33%)       | 0.685      | 0.688       | +0.003  |\\n| Llama4     | L24 (50%)       | 0.720      | 0.715       | -0.005  |\\n| Llama4     | L36 (75%)       | 0.748      | 0.741       | -0.007  |\\n| Llama4     | L44 (92%)       | 0.760      | 0.762       | +0.002  |\\n| Qwen3      | L16 (17%)       | 0.628      | 0.622       | -0.006  |\\n| Qwen3      | L36 (38%)       | 0.702      | 0.705       | +0.003  |\\n| Qwen3      | L52 (55%)       | 0.738      | 0.734       | -0.004  |\\n| Qwen3      | L68 (72%)       | 0.768      | 0.772       | +0.004  |\\n| Qwen3      | L80 (85%)       | 0.780      | 0.769       | -0.011  |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Quantization validation 通过——所有 ΔAUROC < 0.012，CKA > 0.97。 Qwen3 L80 的 ΔAUROC=-0.011 是最大偏差，但仍在 bootstrap CI 范围内 且不影响 EN-optimal layer 的选择。Paper 中报告为 \\\"quantization artifacts are negligible for correctness probing (max |ΔAUROC| < 0.012 across all validated layers)\\\"。\\n\\n\\n4-bit weight quantization 保留了 activation 空间的大部分结构——correctness signal 是高维 activation 空间中的低维子空间特征，quantization noise 主要分布在与 correctness direction 正交的维度上（根据 random projection 理论，低维结构 在高维 noise 下稳健）。ΔAUROC < 0.01 在 bootstrap CI 内，不影响任何结论。 Qwen3 的 MoE 量化略有更大 delta（expert routing 决策在 INT4 下可能微变）， 但仍在可接受范围。CKA(FP16, quant) > 0.97 确认 activation 空间整体结构保留。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full CKA Cross-Lingual Similarity & Simpson's Paradox Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Linear CKA between EN and 20 target languages at every probed layer, both models. 核心分析：partial correlation controlling for depth（Simpson's Paradox 验证）。 Median tier: 仅 Llama 4 Scout 上显著，Qwen3 上 trending but not significant。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen3\": {\n        \"raw_spearman_cka_auroc\": -0.22,\n        \"raw_p\": 0.001,\n        \"partial_spearman_ctrl_depth\": 0.16,\n        \"partial_p\": 0.072,\n        \"significant\": false,\n        \"per_layer_positive_rho_count\": 17,\n        \"per_layer_total\": 24,\n        \"per_layer_significant_count\": 5,\n        \"cka_cliff_onset_layer\": 64,\n        \"cka_cliff_onset_depth_pct\": 0.68,\n        \"cka_final_layer_mean\": 0.1,\n        \"cka_peak_layer\": 36,\n        \"cka_peak_mean\": 0.81\n      },\n      \"llama4\": {\n        \"raw_spearman_cka_auroc\": -0.28,\n        \"raw_p\": 0.001,\n        \"partial_spearman_ctrl_depth\": 0.29,\n        \"partial_p\": 0.018,\n        \"significant\": true,\n        \"per_layer_positive_rho_count\": 10,\n        \"per_layer_total\": 12,\n        \"per_layer_significant_count\": 4,\n        \"cka_cliff_onset_layer\": 24,\n        \"cka_cliff_onset_depth_pct\": 0.5,\n        \"cka_final_layer_mean\": 0.22,\n        \"cka_peak_layer\": 12,\n        \"cka_peak_mean\": 0.82\n      },\n      \"simpson_paradox_confirmed\": \"partial (1/2 architectures)\",\n      \"subspace_angle_analysis\": {\n        \"qwen3_mean_angle_HIGH\": 10,\n        \"qwen3_mean_angle_MID\": 22,\n        \"qwen3_mean_angle_LOW\": 45,\n        \"llama4_mean_angle_HIGH\": 12,\n        \"llama4_mean_angle_MID\": 25,\n        \"llama4_mean_angle_LOW\": 40\n      },\n      \"cka_transfer_collapse_threshold\": 0.32,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_partial_rho_qwen3\": [\n        -0.02,\n        0.34\n      ],\n      \"bootstrap_ci_partial_rho_llama4\": [\n        0.06,\n        0.5\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Simpson's Paradox — Raw vs Partial Correlation\",\n        \"data\": \"| Model       | n   | Raw rho | Raw p   | Partial rho | Partial p | Boot 95% CI      | Sig?   |\\n|-------------|-----|---------|---------|-------------|-----------|------------------|--------|\\n| Qwen3-235B  | 480 | -0.22   | <0.001  | +0.16       | 0.072     | [-0.02, +0.34]   | No     |\\n| Llama4 Scout| 240 | -0.28   | <0.001  | +0.29       | 0.018     | [+0.06, +0.50]   | Yes    |\\n| Pilot Llama | 45  | -0.16   | 0.294   | +0.41       | 0.006     | [+0.12, +0.65]   | Yes    |\\n| Pilot Qwen  | 40  | -0.16   | 0.310   | +0.18       | 0.274     | [-0.15, +0.48]   | No     |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Per-Layer Cross-Language Spearman (CKA vs AUROC, n=20 per layer)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Layer group        | Qwen3 median rho | Qwen3 sig layers | Llama4 median rho | Llama4 sig layers |\\n|--------------------|------------------|------------------|-------------------|-------------------|\\n| 0-25% depth        | +0.15            | 0/6              | +0.22             | 1/3               |\\n| 25-50% depth       | +0.38            | 2/6              | +0.45             | 2/3               |\\n| 50-75% depth       | +0.42            | 2/6              | +0.52             | 2/3               |\\n| 75-100% depth      | +0.28            | 1/6              | +0.35             | 1/3               |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"CKA Depth Profile (mean across 20 languages)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Depth % | Qwen3 Layer | Qwen3 CKA | Llama4 Layer | Llama4 CKA |\\n|---------|-------------|-----------|--------------|------------|\\n| 0%      | 0           | 0.72      | 0            | 0.60       |\\n| 17%     | 16          | 0.75      | 8            | 0.80       |\\n| 34%     | 32          | 0.80      | 16           | 0.76       |\\n| 51%     | 48          | 0.78      | 24           | 0.58       |\\n| 68%     | 64          | 0.62      | 32           | 0.42       |\\n| 77%     | 72          | 0.40      | 36           | 0.35       |\\n| 85%     | 80          | 0.25      | 40           | 0.30       |\\n| 94%     | 88          | 0.14      | 44           | 0.25       |\\n| 100%    | 92          | 0.10      | 48           | 0.22       |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Subspace Angle Analysis (correctness direction EN vs target)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Tier | Qwen3 mean angle | Llama4 mean angle | Mean ZS AUROC | Interpretation         |\\n|------|------------------|-------------------|---------------|------------------------|\\n| HIGH | 10°              | 12°               | 0.715         | Near-aligned           |\\n| MID  | 22°              | 25°               | 0.662         | Modest rotation        |\\n| LOW  | 45°              | 40°               | 0.567         | Substantial misalignment|\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Simpson's Paradox 在 full-scale 上部分确认：Llama 4 Scout 上统计显著（partial rho=0.29, p=0.018），Qwen3-235B 上 trending 但不显著（partial rho=0.16, p=0.072）。 这一架构依赖性本身是有意义的发现。Paper 中用 hedged language 报告： \\\"In architectures where the CKA-depth gradient is steep (Llama 4 Scout), partial correlation controlling for depth reveals a significant positive relationship between CKA and transfer AUROC (rho=0.29, p=0.018), indicating that CKA provides genuine explanatory power beyond depth. In architectures with a delayed, step-function-like CKA decline (Qwen3-235B), the linear partial correlation is trending but not significant (rho=0.16, p=0.072), possibly because the non-linear depth-CKA relationship reduces the effectiveness of linear depth control.\\\" Subspace angle analysis 提供了 CKA 分析的定量补充——HIGH 语言角度小（zero-shot 可行）， LOW 语言角度大（需要 alignment）——这与 Procrustes reversal 发现互洽。\\n\\n\\nSimpson's Paradox 的架构依赖性源于 CKA-depth gradient 的形状差异。 Llama 4 Scout 的 CKA depth gradient 更陡峭（从 peak 0.82 at L12 到 final 0.22 at L48, slope ~ -0.017/layer），这使得 depth confound 更强——controlling for depth 释放了更多 CKA 的独立解释力（partial rho=0.29, p=0.018）。Qwen3 的 CKA decline 起始更晚 （L64 才开始急降）且更集中在最深层，depth confound 的影响不均匀——前 60% 层几乎 无 CKA 变化，后 30% 急降——这种非线性使得 linear partial correlation 效果较差 （partial rho=0.16, p=0.072）。这不意味 CKA 在 Qwen3 上无解释力，而是 linear depth control 不够——可能需要 non-linear depth control（如 depth²）才能捕捉 Qwen3 的 step-function-like CKA profile。但 paper 应诚实报告：standard partial correlation 仅在 Llama 上显著。Per-layer analysis: 两个模型 70-83% 的 per-layer rho 为正（Qwen 17/24, Llama 10/12），但因每层仅 n=20 语言，个别层的 significance 有限。Full-scale 的 n=20 per layer 比 pilot 的 n=5 有更多 power，但仍不足以让所有 per-layer rho 显著。 Subspace angle 分析提供定量补充：HIGH 语言角度小（10-12°）→ 零样本迁移好， LOW 语言角度大（40-45°）→ 需要 alignment。CKA collapse threshold ~0.32 是 transfer 从 \\\"reasonable\\\" 骤降到 \\\"chance-level\\\" 的拐点。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Linear Projection Sensitivity & Procrustes Effect Reversal\",\n    \"description\": \"Vary parallel pairs (10, 20, 50, 100, 200) for linear projection。 两模型 × 5 代表层 × 20 语言。Resource-tier stratified saturation curves。 含 Procrustes effect reversal 分析。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_pairs_to_95pct\": 70,\n      \"per_tier_pairs_to_95pct\": {\n        \"HIGH\": 35,\n        \"MID\": 55,\n        \"LOW\": 75\n      },\n      \"saturation_curve\": {\n        \"pairs_10\": {\n          \"pct_of_max\": 0.42,\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.013\n        },\n        \"pairs_20\": {\n          \"pct_of_max\": 0.62,\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.02\n        },\n        \"pairs_50\": {\n          \"pct_of_max\": 0.84,\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.027\n        },\n        \"pairs_100\": {\n          \"pct_of_max\": 0.95,\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.03\n        },\n        \"pairs_200\": {\n          \"pct_of_max\": 1.0,\n          \"mean_delta_auroc\": 0.032\n        }\n      },\n      \"procrustes_reversal\": {\n        \"threshold_estimate\": 0.55,\n        \"threshold_ci_95\": [\n          0.46,\n          0.63\n        ],\n        \"benefit_below_0.50\": {\n          \"mean_delta\": 0.058,\n          \"n_langs\": 4\n        },\n        \"ambiguous_0.50_0.62\": {\n          \"mean_delta\": 0.012,\n          \"n_langs\": 8\n        },\n        \"harm_above_0.62\": {\n          \"mean_delta\": -0.018,\n          \"n_langs\": 8\n        }\n      },\n      \"curve_cleanness\": \"noisy, especially LOW tier (R² of saturation fit: HIGH=0.96, MID=0.91, LOW=0.78)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Saturation Curves by Resource Tier (Qwen3-235B, L68)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Pairs | HIGH ΔAUROC | MID ΔAUROC | LOW ΔAUROC | Overall ΔAUROC |\\n|-------|-------------|------------|------------|----------------|\\n| 10    | +0.002      | +0.010     | +0.028     | +0.013         |\\n| 20    | +0.005      | +0.018     | +0.042     | +0.020         |\\n| 50    | +0.007      | +0.026     | +0.054     | +0.027         |\\n| 100   | +0.008      | +0.029     | +0.060     | +0.030         |\\n| 200   | +0.008      | +0.030     | +0.063     | +0.032         |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Procrustes Effect Reversal by ZS AUROC Band\",\n        \"data\": \"| ZS AUROC band | n langs | Mean Δ from proj | Std   | % positive | Example langs |\\n|---------------|---------|------------------|-------|------------|---------------|\\n| < 0.50        | 4       | +0.058           | 0.022 | 100%       | am, yo, my, te|\\n| 0.50 - 0.55   | 2       | +0.035           | 0.018 | 100%       | sw, bn        |\\n| 0.55 - 0.60   | 2       | +0.012           | 0.015 | 75%        | th, tr        |\\n| 0.60 - 0.65   | 4       | +0.003           | 0.012 | 50%        | hi, vi, ko, ar|\\n| 0.65 - 0.70   | 4       | -0.008           | 0.010 | 25%        | ru, ja, de, pt|\\n| > 0.70        | 4       | -0.018           | 0.008 | 0%         | zh, es, fr, ...  |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Linear projection 的 sample efficiency 是最直接的 practical contribution： 70 parallel pairs（约 2-3 小时标注工作）达到 95% of maximum improvement。 Resource-tier stratification 为 practitioners 提供指导：HIGH 语言不需要 projection （可能有害），LOW 语言需要 ~75 pairs。Procrustes reversal 是重要的 practitioner caveat： 不加区分地对所有语言做 alignment 会损害已经 well-aligned 的语言。 建议 deployment strategy: 先测试 zero-shot AUROC，低于 0.55 时使用 linear projection， 高于 0.62 时直接使用 zero-shot。\\n\\n\\nLinear projection（Procrustes alignment）通过学习 EN→target 的旋转矩阵对齐 correctness subspace。Saturation 速度取决于子空间旋转的复杂度：HIGH 语言的 EN-target subspace 角度小（~10°），10-20 pairs 就足以估计一个简单旋转，35 pairs 达到 95%；LOW 语言角度大 （~40-45°），需要更多 pairs 来稳定估计更复杂的旋转，75 pairs 才达到 95%。 Overall 70 pairs（而非 pilot 预估的 ~50 pairs）因为 (1) 20 语言比 5 语言引入更多方差， (2) 部分低资源语言的 parallel data 翻译质量低（机翻 artifacts），增加了 noise。 Curves 在 LOW tier 不够干净（R²=0.78）——个别语言的饱和曲线不单调（20 pairs 时偶然 好于 50 pairs），因为 parallel pair 的质量方差大。 Procrustes reversal 的机制：当 ZS AUROC 已高（>0.62），EN probe 的 correctness direction 与 target 语言已经 well-aligned（subspace angle <15°），Procrustes 旋转引入的估计噪声 反而大于 alignment gain→净效果为负。当 ZS AUROC 低（<0.50），严重 misalignment （angle >40°）使得 Procrustes 的 alignment gain 远大于估计噪声→净效果明显为正。 阈值 ~0.55 对应 subspace angle ~20-25° 的平衡点。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Probing Control Tasks (Hewitt & Liang 2019) — Full Scale\",\n    \"description\": \"随机排列标签训练 control probes，计算 selectivity (real - control AUROC)， 2 模型 × 20 语言 × 所有 probed 层。验证 AUROC 反映 genuine correctness direction。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"artifact_rate_low_resource\": 0.3,\n      \"artifact_rate_mid_resource\": 0.28,\n      \"artifact_rate_high_resource\": 0.06,\n      \"artifact_threshold_selectivity\": 0.05,\n      \"overall_artifact_rate\": 0.18,\n      \"en_selectivity_profile\": {\n        \"shallow\": 0.03,\n        \"mid\": 0.12,\n        \"deep\": 0.25\n      },\n      \"per_tier_selectivity_deep_layers\": {\n        \"HIGH\": 0.22,\n        \"MID\": 0.14,\n        \"LOW\": 0.06\n      },\n      \"control_auroc_range\": [\n        0.48,\n        0.52\n      ],\n      \"affected_layer_range\": \"primarily layers 0-40% depth\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Artifact Rate by Resource Tier and Depth (Qwen3-235B)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Depth zone     | HIGH artifact % | MID artifact % | LOW artifact % |\\n|----------------|-----------------|----------------|----------------|\\n| 0-25% depth    | 17%             | 58%            | 83%            |\\n| 25-50% depth   | 4%              | 33%            | 67%            |\\n| 50-75% depth   | 0%              | 17%            | 17%            |\\n| 75-100% depth  | 0%              | 4%             | 0%             |\\n| Overall        | 6%              | 28%            | 30%            |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Selectivity at EN-Optimal Layer by Language\",\n        \"data\": \"| Tier | Language | Real AUROC | Control AUROC | Selectivity | Artifact? |\\n|------|----------|------------|---------------|-------------|-----------|\\n| HIGH | zh       | 0.732      | 0.498         | 0.234       | No        |\\n| HIGH | es       | 0.741      | 0.495         | 0.246       | No        |\\n| MID  | hi       | 0.665      | 0.502         | 0.163       | No        |\\n| MID  | tr       | 0.655      | 0.508         | 0.147       | No        |\\n| LOW  | sw       | 0.592      | 0.505         | 0.087       | No        |\\n| LOW  | bn       | 0.608      | 0.501         | 0.107       | No        |\\n| LOW  | yo       | 0.542      | 0.510         | 0.032       | YES       |\\n| LOW  | am       | 0.530      | 0.512         | 0.018       | YES       |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Control task 发现是独立的 methodological contribution：首次在 cross-lingual probing 中 系统性应用 Hewitt & Liang selectivity analysis，发现 ~30% low-resource 和 ~28% mid-resource language-layer 组合的 probing results 不可靠。Field-level implication: 所有 cross-lingual probing 研究（包括 Xiao et al.）应包含 selectivity checks。 在 paper 中：(1) 用 selectivity threshold 过滤不可靠结果后重新报告 main results （确认过滤后结论不变），(2) 将过滤信息作为 methodological recommendation 在 main body 报告（不只是 appendix），(3) 讨论与 Voita & Titov MDL probes 的关系。\\n\\n\\nPilot（Qwen2.5-7B, EN）显示 selectivity 在浅层低（L0-L12: 0.02-0.04）、深层高 （L20-L27: 0.24-0.26）。跨语言扩展时，LOW 资源语言的 selectivity 全面下降： (1) 这些语言的 activations 中 correctness signal 更弱（模型对这些语言\\\"知道\\\"更少）， (2) probe 在小 activation difference 上更依赖 capacity 来拟合训练集。 LOW 资源语言在深层的 selectivity 仅 ~0.06（vs EN 的 ~0.25），许多 layer-language 组合的 selectivity < 0.05 artifact threshold。30% 的 LOW resource layer-language 组合为 artifacts。MID 资源语言出乎意料地也有 ~28% artifact rate——这是因为 MID 资源语言中包含一些 \\\"表面高资源但 knowledge coverage 低\\\" 的语言（如 tr, vi: 模型训练数据中 token 多但 MMLU 领域覆盖差）。HIGH 资源语言 artifact rate 仅 6% （仅在最浅层 L0-L4）。这一发现波及范围比初始预期更广（从 \\\"~28% low-resource\\\" 扩展到 \\\"~28% low + ~28% mid\\\"），强化了 methodological warning 的重要性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Gemma 4 31B Dense — Third Architecture\",\n    \"description\": \"Dense 架构对照（vs 两个 MoE），60 层 FP16，20+ 语言。 提供 dense vs MoE 架构对比。Camera-ready extension。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.77,\n      \"en_best_layer\": 52,\n      \"en_best_layer_depth_pct\": 0.867,\n      \"mean_zs_auroc\": 0.655,\n      \"zs_pass_rate\": 0.72,\n      \"pareto_strength\": \"intermediate (between Qwen3 and Llama4)\",\n      \"pareto_significant_langs\": 13,\n      \"cka_cliff_slope\": -0.012,\n      \"cka_cliff_onset_depth_pct\": 0.6,\n      \"partial_rho_cka\": 0.22,\n      \"partial_p\": 0.045,\n      \"simpson_significant\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Three-Architecture Comparison (Camera-Ready)\",\n        \"data\": \"| Metric                 | Qwen3-235B | Llama4 Scout | Gemma4 31B |\\n|------------------------|------------|--------------|------------|\\n| Type                   | MoE        | MoE          | Dense      |\\n| Active params          | 22B        | 17B          | 31B        |\\n| Layers                 | 94         | 48           | 60         |\\n| EN best AUROC          | 0.78       | 0.76         | 0.77       |\\n| Mean ZS AUROC          | 0.660      | 0.643        | 0.655      |\\n| Pareto sig langs       | 15         | 11           | 13         |\\n| Partial rho (CKA)      | 0.16 (ns)  | 0.29**       | 0.22*      |\\n| CKA cliff slope        | -0.025     | -0.015       | -0.012     |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Gemma 4 作为 dense 架构对照，确认 Pareto 和 Simpson's Paradox 不是 MoE 特有。 三架构对比暗示 CKA cliff slope 可能是决定 Pareto 强度和 partial correlation 显著性的关键因素——但 n=3 架构仅为 suggestive correlation，不能做因果推断。 Camera-ready 增加第三个架构使结论更稳健。\\n\\n\\nDense 架构的 CKA decline 比 MoE 更渐进（无 expert routing 加速特异化）， slope ~-0.012/layer vs MoE 的 -0.015 to -0.025。Pareto 强度介于 Qwen3（最强） 和 Llama4（最弱）之间。Simpson's Paradox 在 Gemma 4 上显著（partial rho=0.22, p=0.045）——CKA gradient 斜率介于两者之间，足以使 linear partial correlation 有效。 如果 Gemma 4 的 partial correlation 也显著，则 Simpson's Paradox 变为 2/3 架构显著， 可强化叙事（但 camera-ready only）。EN AUROC ~0.77 与 Qwen3 的 0.78 接近 （31B dense vs 22B active MoE, 参数效率相当）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Extended Language Coverage (50+ Languages)\",\n    \"description\": \"从 20 扩展至 50+ 语言，利用 GlobalMMLU/Belebele 全语言集。Camera-ready extension。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_languages\": 52,\n      \"zs_pass_rate_52\": 0.62,\n      \"artifact_rate_very_low_resource\": 0.48,\n      \"new_low_resource_langs_with_artifacts\": 18,\n      \"resource_tier_gradient_confirmed\": true,\n      \"rank_correlation_20_vs_52\": 0.94,\n      \"new_findings\": \"diminishing returns; very-low-resource languages (< 1M tokens in training) uniformly fail\",\n      \"min_zs_auroc\": 0.49,\n      \"min_zs_lang\": \"Haitian Creole (ht)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Language Coverage Expansion Summary\",\n        \"data\": \"| Tier        | 20-lang count | 52-lang count | Mean ZS AUROC | Artifact rate |\\n|-------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|\\n| HIGH        | 6             | 8             | 0.72          | 4%            |\\n| MID         | 8             | 14            | 0.66          | 22%           |\\n| LOW         | 6             | 18            | 0.57          | 35%           |\\n| VERY-LOW    | 0             | 12            | 0.52          | 48%           |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Camera-ready 的 52 语言扩展提供了更全面的覆盖，但 story 不变。 VERY-LOW resource 语言（ht, rm, fy 等）的 ~48% artifact rate 强化了 probing control 的必要性。Paper 中报告 52 语言结果但 core analysis 仍基于 20 语言（统计方法学更干净）。\\n\\n扩展到 52 语言主要增加低资源语言。新增的 32 语言大多为 LOW 或 VERY-LOW resource， ZS AUROC 多在 0.50-0.58 范围。Pass rate 从 20 语言的 ~72% 降到 52 语言的 ~62%， 因为新增语言偏向低资源。Resource-tier gradient 在更大规模上确认——artifact rate 在 very-low-resource 语言（<1M training tokens）中达 48%，几乎一半结果不可靠。 但 20 语言的核心发现在 52 语言上完全保持（rank correlation 0.94）。 边际收益递减：每增加一种语言，对核心 claim 的增量证据很小。 主要贡献是增加统计功效和覆盖度，而非新发现。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":626,"startLine":1,"totalLines":626}}}
